21115794,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"This paper does not report sequences from patient samples. The study focuses on the virological and pharmacological properties of S/GSK1349572, a next-generation HIV integrase inhibitor, without detailing the sequencing of HIV samples from patients.","The content of the paper primarily discusses the in vitro and cellular assays involving HIV-1 strains, integrase inhibition, and drug resistance mechanisms of S/GSK1349572. There is no mention of obtaining HIV sequences from patient samples, nor is there any demographic information about patients included in the materials and methods."
21115794,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"S/GSK1349572 was evaluated against molecular clones with mutations in the integrase-, RT-, and protease-coding regions. INI-, NRTI-, and NNRTI-resistant mutants were analyzed by the reporter assays based on HeLa-CD4 cells, while PI-resistant mutants were analyzed by infectivity in MT-4 cells, with monitoring of RT activity as described previously.","The study includes in vitro assays demonstrating the antiviral activity of S/GSK1349572 against various HIV strains and resistant mutants, indicating that drug susceptibility data were collected through these assays."
21115794,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,No evidence,"The paper does not mention the public release of any sequences, nor does it provide any GenBank accession numbers, which indicates that the sequences were not made publicly available."
