25637519,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"Mutation D404N, alone or together with the other reported mutations, was introduced into an HIV-1 CRF08_BC subtype infectious clone by site-directed mutagenesis. The WT infectious plasmid pBRGX was constructed and confirmed from a clinical isolate of CRF08_BC subtype in our previous study.","The paper describes the introduction of mutations into an HIV-1 CRF08_BC subtype infectious clone and does not mention obtaining HIV sequences from patient samples. The focus is on laboratory-based studies using constructed virus mutants, and there is no indication that sequences from patient samples were reported."
25637519,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"Phenotypic drug susceptibility of the virus mutants. The susceptibility of the mutant viruses to NNRTIs (nevirapine, efavirenz, etravirine and rilpivirine) and NRTIs (zidovudine, abacavir sulphate, lamivudine, emtricitabine and tenofovir disoproxil fumarate) was measured in a single-cycle cell-culture-based phenotypic assay as described previously.  Phenotypic analysis of the susceptibility of virus variants to RT inhibitors: (a) nevirapine (NVP), (b) efavirenz (EFV), (c) etravirine (ETR), (d) rilpivirine (RPV) and (e) NRTIs (ZDV, zidovudine; ABC, abacavir sulphate; 3TC, lamivudine; FTC, emtricitabine; TDF, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate).",The paper reports in vitro drug susceptibility data by measuring the susceptibility of mutant viruses to various RT inhibitors and NRTIs in a single-cycle cell-culture-based phenotypic assay. The data is presented in figures and described in the methods and results sections.
