28559249,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,MK-8591 also retains potent activity against multinucleoside-resistant HIV-2 mutants (EC50 ≤ 11 nM). These data suggest that MK-8591 may have antiviral activity in HIV-2-infected individuals.,"The paper primarily focuses on the in vitro activity of the investigational compound MK-8591 against HIV-2 isolates and drug-resistant HIV-2 mutants. It does not mention obtaining HIV sequences from patient samples or provide any details regarding the sequencing of HIV from patient samples. The emphasis is on the drug's efficacy and mechanisms rather than on sequencing data from patients. Therefore, the paper does not report HIV sequences from patient samples."
28559249,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"MK-8591 (4′-ethynyl-2-fluoro-2′-deoxyadenosine [EFdA]) exhibits potent activity against HIV-2 isolates and drug-resistant HIV-2 mutants in culture; 50% effective concentrations (EC50) for HIV-2 were, on average, 4.8-fold lower than those observed for HIV-1.","The paper reports the in vitro drug susceptibility data of MK-8591 against various HIV-1 and HIV-2 strains. The EC50 values indicating the effective concentrations of the drug against these isolates are detailed in the results of the study. This is a direct indication that in vitro susceptibility data is being presented in the paper, as it discusses the effectiveness of the drug on cultured cells infected with HIV-1 and HIV-2."
28559249,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,MK-8591 also retains potent activity against multinucleoside-resistant HIV-2 mutants (EC50 ≤ 11 nM). These data suggest that MK-8591 may have antiviral activity in HIV-2-infected individuals.,The paper does not mention that any sequences obtained were made publicly available. It focuses on the experimental results of the drug's efficacy rather than on sequencing data.
28559249,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not reported,"In the present study, we tested the activity of MK-8591 against a panel of HIV-1 and HIV-2 strains that were originally isolated from ART-naive individuals. To our knowledge, this remains the only report of an NRTI that, when tested against a diverse panel of HIV-1 and HIV-2 isolates, exhibits more-potent inhibition of HIV-2 replication.","The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates, as the primary focus is on the drug's activity against HIV-1 and HIV-2 strains rather than on sequencing data."
