30053052,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,No evidence,No evidence,The paper does not detail the specific drugs received by individuals prior to sample sequencing.
30803972,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"We compared the activity of the integrase inhibitor bictegravir against HIV-1 and HIV-2 using a culture-based, single-cycle assay. Values of 50% effective concentrations ranged from 1.2 to 2.5 nM for 9 HIV-1 isolates and 1.4 to 5.6 nM for 15 HIV-2 isolates.",The paper focuses on the in vitro activity of the drug bictegravir against HIV-1 and HIV-2 isolates and does not mention obtaining HIV sequences from patient samples.
30803972,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"We compared the activity of the integrase inhibitor bictegravir against HIV-1 and HIV-2 using a culture-based, single-cycle assay. Values of 50% effective concentrations ranged from 1.2 to 2.5 nM for 9 HIV-1 isolates and 1.4 to 5.6 nM for 15 HIV-2 isolates.","The paper reports in vitro drug susceptibility data, specifically detailing the effective concentrations of the integrase inhibitor bictegravir against various HIV-1 and HIV-2 isolates in a laboratory setting."
30803972,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"We compared the activity of the integrase inhibitor bictegravir against HIV-1 and HIV-2 using a culture-based, single-cycle assay. Values of 50% effective concentrations ranged from 1.2 to 2.5 nM for 9 HIV-1 isolates and 1.4 to 5.6 nM for 15 HIV-2 isolates.","The paper does not mention any public availability of sequences, focusing instead on in vitro studies of drug effectiveness."
30803972,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No nucleotides,"We compared the activity of the integrase inhibitor bictegravir against HIV-1 and HIV-2 using a culture-based, single-cycle assay. Values of 50% effective concentrations ranged from 1.2 to 2.5 nM for 9 HIV-1 isolates and 1.4 to 5.6 nM for 15 HIV-2 isolates.","The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates, as it does not report on sequencing."
30803972,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,0,"We compared the activity of the integrase inhibitor bictegravir against HIV-1 and HIV-2 using a culture-based, single-cycle assay. Values of 50% effective concentrations ranged from 1.2 to 2.5 nM for 9 HIV-1 isolates and 1.4 to 5.6 nM for 15 HIV-2 isolates.","The paper does not mention any individuals from whom samples were obtained for HIV sequencing, as it focuses on in vitro assays."
