om which sequenced samples were obtained, as it does not report any patient-derived sequences. The study was conducted using laboratory strains and recombinant viruses."
34516245,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,Yes,"In addition to population sequencing, clonal sequencing was also performed to confirm the identity of the HIV-1 RT mutants ( Table 1 and Fig. 5 ). Radiolabeled dinucleotide RT assays confirmed that K65R isolated during passaging had reverted back to wild-type (WT) HIV-1 ( Table 1 and Fig. 5A ). We confirm that M184V and M184I arise, at least in part, by genetic drift during passage and that K65R is lost after P4, verified by clonal sequencing. In addition, we previously reported that the population sequencing methods were not capable of detecting resistant mutants emerging in the K65R, M184V, and D67N/K70R/T215F/K219Q backgrounds during selection of NRTI drugs (13, 16, 47 [52] ). Radioactive sequencing of infected primary CD4+ T cells demonstrated that as little as 0.3% of M184V could be shown using clonal methods (34).","The paper mentions clonal sequencing were performed to confirm the identity of the mutants, indicating that samples were cloned prior to sequencing."
