35730213,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"Abstract

HIV programmes across many countries in Africa have recently transitioned people living with HIV from efavirenz (EFV)- to dolutegravir (DTG)-containing antiretroviral therapy (ART). As both drugs are associated with neuropsychiatric adverse effects, this study assessed the mental health and HIV/ART-associated symptoms of people living with HIV before and after transition to DTG.

Methods

The prospective DO-REAL cohort enrolled people starting DTG-based ART in Lesotho from February to December 2020. For this analysis within DO-REAL, we included adults changing from tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF)/lamivudine (3TC)/EFV to TDF/3TC/DTG within first-line therapy. At transition and 16 weeks thereafter, participants completed the Patient Health Questionnaire-9 (PHQ-9; depression screening), the 12-item Short-Form Health Survey (SF-12; mental and physical health), and a modified HIV Symptom Index (mHSI; HIV/ART-related symptoms). We also assessed weight change. We used McNemar tests with Bonferroni corrections to assess binary outcomes. ClinicalTrials.gov : NCT04238767.",The paper does not mention any sequencing of HIV from patient samples. The focus is on the mental health and ART-associated symptoms of people living with HIV who transitioned to dolutegravir-based therapy. The study design and methods described do not involve obtaining or analyzing HIV sequences from patient samples.
35730213,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Methods

The prospective DO-REAL cohort enrolled people starting DTG-based ART in Lesotho from February to December 2020. For this analysis within DO-REAL, we included adults changing from tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF)/lamivudine (3TC)/EFV to TDF/3TC/DTG within first-line therapy. At transition and 16 weeks thereafter, participants completed the Patient Health Questionnaire-9 (PHQ-9; depression screening), the 12-item Short-Form Health Survey (SF-12; mental and physical health), and a modified HIV Symptom Index (mHSI; HIV/ART-related symptoms). We also assessed weight change. We used McNemar tests with Bonferroni corrections to assess binary outcomes. ClinicalTrials.gov : NCT04238767.","The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data. The focus is on the mental health and HIV/ART-associated symptoms of people living with HIV who transitioned to dolutegravir-based therapy, and the methods described do not involve in vitro susceptibility testing."
