Methods. Eligibility criteria included need for parenteral therapy, no primary resistance mutations to cabotegravir or rilpivirine, and established retention in care. Demographic, efficacy, and safety data were obtained from standardized programme applications and quarterly clinical updates.","The paper does not mention any HIV sequences obtained from patient samples. It focuses on the compassionate use of a treatment regimen and reports on demographic, efficacy, and safety data, but there is no indication that HIV sequences were analyzed or reported."
35945163,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"ABSTRACT; Objectives. Physicians could request compassionate use of oral and long-acting (LA) cabotegravir + rilpivirine for people living with HIV-1 under a single-patient request programme supported by ViiV Healthcare and Janssen. Outcomes are reported. Methods. Eligibility criteria included need for parenteral therapy, no primary resistance mutations to cabotegravir or rilpivirine, and established retention in care. Demographic, efficacy, and safety data were obtained from standardized programme applications and quarterly clinical updates. Individuals received a loading dose of LA cabotegravir 600 mg + rilpivirine 900 mg, followed by LA maintenance doses of 400 mg/600 mg every 4 weeks; some received lead-in oral cabotegravir and rilpivirine.",The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data. It focuses on the compassionate use treatment outcomes of a specific antiretroviral regimen and does not include any laboratory-based susceptibility testing results.
35945163,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"Methods. Eligibility criteria included need for parenteral therapy, no primary resistance mutations to cabotegravir or rilpivirine, and established retention in care. Demographic, efficacy, and safety data were obtained from standardized programme applications and quarterly clinical updates. Individuals received a loading dose of LA cabotegravir 600 mg + rilpivirine 900 mg, followed by LA maintenance doses of 400 mg/600 mg every 4 weeks; some received lead-in oral cabotegravir and rilpivirine. Compassionate use programmes were conducted in accordance with local regulatory guidelines for the UK, the USA, Belgium, Canada, Netherlands, Switzerland, Portugal, Italy, South Korea, and Spain, each of which had participating people living with HIV-1.","The paper does not mention any publicly available sequences. It focuses on the compassionate use program and reports on treatment outcomes, demographic data, and safety, but there is no mention of sequence data being made publicly available."
