35945163,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"ABSTRACT; Objectives. Physicians could request compassionate use of oral and long-acting (LA) cabotegravir + rilpivirine for people living with HIV-1 under a single-patient request programme supported by ViiV Healthcare and Janssen. Outcomes are reported. Methods. Eligibility criteria included need for parenteral therapy, no primary resistance mutations to cabotegravir or rilpivirine, and established retention in care. Demographic, efficacy, and safety data were obtained from standardized programme applications and quarterly clinical updates. Individuals received a loading dose of LA cabotegravir 600 mg + rilpivirine 900 mg, followed by LA maintenance doses of 400 mg/600 mg every 4 weeks; some received lead-in oral cabotegravir and rilpivirine. COMPASSIONATE USE—CABOTEGRAVIR LA, RILPIVIRINE LA 4 Therapeutic Advances in Infectious Disease 8 programme from February 2016 through July 2020. Included individuals from 10 countries, including 12 from the United Kingdom; 11 from the United States; two each from Belgium, Canada, Netherlands, and Switzerland; and one each from Portugal, Italy, South Korea, and Spain. Of the people living with HIV-1 included, 57% were female, 31% were perinatally infected, and median age was 36 years (Table 1). The majority of people living with HIV-1 requested compassionate use because of chronic poor adherence to oral ART due to psychological conditions (43%) or physical challenges (23%). Most (66%) people living with HIV-1 received an oral lead-in of cabotegravir + rilpivirine for ∼4 weeks before starting LA dosing; the remaining 34% initiated LA injections without an oral lead-in. Vehicle engulfment (2018) and stability studies (. Outcomes are reported. Methods. Eligibility criteria included need for parenteral therapy, no primary resistance mutations to cabotegravir or rilpivirine, and established retention in care  This paper is focused on treatment outcomes and does not report any virological failure sequences.","The paper does not mention whether any sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen. It focuses on the compassionate use program and treatment outcomes, reports on the reason for use,  efficacy, and safety, but there is no mention of sequencing or obtaining sequences from individuals with virological failure."
35945163,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"Compassionate use programmes facilitate early access to drugs in late-stage clinical development for patients who do not qualify for ongoing registrational studies and have serious or life-threatening conditions with prohibited or limited treatment options.12,13 Compassionate use programmes may also allow access to investigational drugs for patients in countries awaiting regulatory approval of a drug that has already been approved elsewhere. Unlike many other conditions with compassionate use programmes, multiple antiretroviral agents are already approved for the treatment of HIV-1 infection. Moreover, this compassionate use programme is unique in that it not only facilitated early access to the emerging novel treatment paradigm of cabotegravir LA+ rilpivirine LA, the first LA injectable therapy for HIV-1, but it also fulfilled a specific need among people living with HIV-1 who are in need of parenteral ART administration.","The paper describes a compassionate use program, not a clinical trial. It reports on the outcomes of individuals who received treatment outside of a formal clinical trial setting."
