36454248,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"During 2018–19, plasma was collected from 76 HIV-infected children/adolescents (5 ART-naive, 71 treated) in Panama for HIV-1 DRM pol analysis. HIV-1 pol sequences were recovered from 67 (88.2%) of 76 children/adolescents (median age 12 years), carrying 65 subtype B, 1 subtype G and 1 unique recombinant URF_A1B.","The paper describes the collection and analysis of plasma samples from HIV-infected children and adolescents in Panama, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
36454248,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"During 2018--19, plasma was collected from 76 HIV-infected children/adolescents (5 ART-naive, 71 treated) in Panama for HIV-1 DRM pol analysis, predicted antiretroviral (ARV) susceptibility by Stanford, and HIV-1 variant phylogenetic characterization. Resistances to ARVs were identified but not in vitro testing were taken up.","The paper mentions predicted antiretroviral susceptibility, which refers to the expected effectiveness of drugs based on genetic sequencing data, but it does not provide in vitro drug susceptibility data from laboratory experiments."
36454248,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,HIV-1 sequences were submitted to GenBank with the following accession numbers: OM201778 -- OM201846.,"The paper explicitly states that the HIV-1 sequences were submitted to GenBank, indicating that they have been made publicly available."
36454248,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,OM201778 -- OM201846,HIV-1 sequences were submitted to GenBank with the following accession numbers: OM201778 -- OM201846.,"The paper provides the specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, confirming their public availability."
36454248,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,76,"During 2018--19, plasma was collected from 76 HIV-infected children/adolescents (5 ART-naive, 71 treated) in Panama for HIV-1 DRM pol analysis. Plasma samples from 76 HIV-positive naive or ART-treated children and adolescents with therapeutic failure under clinical follow-up at this hospital were collected during 2018--19.","The paper states that plasma samples were collected from 76 HIV-infected children and adolescents for the study, indicating the number of individuals whose samples were obtained for sequencing."
36454248,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Panama,"Plasma was collected from 76 HIV-infected children/adolescents (5 ART-naive, 71 treated) in Panama for HIV-1 DRM pol analysis. This study provides the most recent data on resistance to ARVs among HIV-infected children and adolescents in Panama and it is the first to report resistance data for INSTIs in Panama, which is appropriate after the broad implementation of dolutegravir.","The paper specifies that the samples were collected from HIV-infected children and adolescents in Panama, indicating the country of origin for the sequenced samples."
36454248,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2018-2019,"During 2018–19, plasma was collected from 76 HIV-infected children/adolescents (5 ART-naive, 71 treated) in Panama for HIV-1 DRM pol analysis. Table ​ Table1 1 summarizes the epidemiological and virological features of the 76 HIV-1-infected children/adolescents that made up the complete study cohort at sampling (2018--19)","The paper mentions that the samples were collected during the years 2018 to 2019, providing a specific time frame for when the sequencing was conducted."
36454248,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"The extracted RNA was amplified by RT--PCR and nested PCR to obtain the HIV-1 *pol* region, using primers designed by WHO for protease (PR) and reverse transcriptase (RT) amplification and ANRS primers for integrase (IN) amplification.","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing, indicating that the samples were directly sequenced without cloning."
36454248,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"PR, RT, IN","HIV-1 RNA was extracted from plasma by automated magnetic silica extraction using the EasyMAG extractor (bioMérieux). The extracted RNA was amplified by RT--PCR and nested PCR to obtain the HIV-1 *pol* region, using primers designed by WHO for protease (PR) and reverse transcriptase (RT) amplification and ANRS primers for integrase (IN) amplification. Table ​ ​ Table1 1 summarizes the epidemiological and virological features of the 76 HIV-1-infected children/adolescents that made up the complete study cohort Parts of the pol region sequenced ranged from PR, RT and IN , not the full genome.","The paper mentions the sequencing of the PR, RT, and IN regions, indicating the specific HIV genes that were reported."
36454248,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Macrogen Inc.,PCR amplicons were purified with illustra TM ExoProStar TM (Cytiva) and sequenced by Macrogen Inc. Lasergene software was used to assemble and manually edit the sequences.,"The paper states that the sequencing was performed by Macrogen Inc, which is a method of Sanger sequencing."
36454248,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"During 2018–19, plasma was collected from 76 HIV-infected children/adolescents (5 ART-naive, 71 treated) in Panama for HIV-1 DRM pol analysis. Plasma samples from 76 HIV-positive naive or ART-treated children and adolescents with therapeutic failure under clinical follow-up at this hospital were collected during 2018--19. The samples were kept at −20°C until transported on dry ice to the HIV-1 Molecular Epidemiology Laboratory in Madrid, Spain, where they were stored at −80°C until processing.","The paper specifies that plasma samples were collected from the HIV-infected children and adolescents, indicating the type of clinical specimens that were sequenced.Plasma samples from 76 HIV-positive naive or ART-treated children and adolescents with therapeutic failure under clinical follow-up at this hospital were collected during 2018--19."
36454248,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"Most (95%) were infected perinatally and all are under ART, 43% of them reaching HIV viral suppression. Plasma samples from 76 HIV-positive naive or ART-treated children and adolescents with therapeutic failure under clinical follow-up at this hospital were collected during 2018--19. All 71 treated children/adolescents had received NRTIs, 45.1% NNRTIs, 95.8% PIs and just 11 (15.5%) patients were INSTI-experienced (Table ​ (Table1). 1 ). At the time of sampling, the basis of paediatric ART in Panama was triple therapy with zidovudine + lamivudine + lopinavir/ritonavir. Most treated children (98.6%) had received lamivudine + zidovudine, followed by lopinavir / ritonavir (95.8%) and efavirenz (45.1%).% had received four to eight different ART regimens at sampling , Most (70.2%) of the 57 subjects with documented data lacked comorbidities.","The paper indicates that all children were under ART Most (70.2%) of the 57 subjects with documented data lacked comorbidities, at least 43% reaching VL suppression, all is annotated under samples sequenced including naieve children 5 in total and 71 experienced children most which indicates that the individuals with virological failure were included."
36454248,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"Plasma samples from 76 HIV-positive naive or ART-treated children and adolescents with therapeutic failure under clinical follow-up at this hospital were collected during 2018--19. Most (95%) were infected perinatally and all are under ART, 43% of them reaching HIV viral suppression; study not a clinical trial.","The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial, it was only a surveillance study."
36454248,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Plasma was collected from 76 HIV-infected children/adolescents (5 ART-naive, 71 treated) in Panama for HIV-1 DRM pol analysis. Most (95%) were infected perinatally and all are under ART, 43% of them reaching HIV viral suppression. All 71 treated children/adolescents had received NRTIs, 45.1% NNRTIs, 95.8% PIs and just 11 (15.5%) patients were INSTI-experienced.","The paper indicates that all childs were on ARV drugs as all were under clinical follow up Most (95%) were infected perinatally and all are under ART, 43% of them reaching HIV viral suppression;"
36454248,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, INSTIs","Plasma was collected from 76 HIV-infected children/adolescents (5 ART-naive, 71 treated) in Panama for HIV-1 DRM pol analysis. Most (95%) were infected perinatally and all are under ART, 43% of them reaching HIV viral suppression. All 71 treated children/adolescents had received NRTIs, 45.1% NNRTIs, 95.8% PIs and just 11 (15.5%) patients were INSTI-experienced.","The paper indicates the kids were on all drug classes NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, INSTIs, as all were under clinical follow up and gained sequencing results."
36454248,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"zidovudine, lamivudine, lopinavir/ritonavir, efavirenz, maraviroc, tenofovir, atazanavir, darunavir raltegravir","Most treated children with available historical ART data had received lamivudine, 3TC, zidovudine, ZDV, but presented high/intermediate resistance mainly to emtricitabine and lamivudine. Tenofovir disoproxil, TDF and efavirenz, marviroc, maraviroc, all with major DRMs and high/intermediat resistance to integrase and PIs. All naive children had received Zidovudine or lamivudine as prophylaxis. Our study found high DRM prevalence among treated subjects, showing that one in two ART-experienced patients under therapeutic failure with available pol sequence carried resistant strains. Experiencing failure on INSTI (11,15.5%) and all had received Raltegravir  , Integration is due to CDC and accepted the use of meraviroc.","The paper mentions the drugs received by the kids under clinical follow up and had sequencing results Most treated children with available historical ART data had received lamivudine, 3TC, zidovudine, ZDV, but presented high/intermediate resistance mainly to emtricitabine and lamivudine."
36519389,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"CHARACTERISE enrolled residents of inner-city Johannesburg from July to November 2022 who had previously been part of ADVANCE and were not pregnant at the time of screening. Participants switching either TAF/FTC + DTG or TDF/FTC/EFV to TDF/3TC/DTG showed statistically significant reductions in weight, low-density lipoprotein, triglycerides, glucose and glycated hemoglobin.",The paper does not mention any HIV sequences from patient samples as it focuses on the metabolic and virological outcomes of different antiretroviral therapy regimens.
36519389,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"In the CHARACTERISE study, participants who switched from TDF/FTC/EFV to TDF/3TC/DTG gained a median 2.9 kg. We also saw small improvements in LDL cholesterol, triglycerides, fasting glucose, and HbA1C during the switches from TDF/FTC/EFV to TDF/3TC/DTG. Again, this change is expected, given the previously described metabolic effects of EFV [4].",The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data as it focuses on the clinical outcomes of switching antiretroviral therapy regimens.
36519389,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"CHARACTERISE enrolled residents of inner-city Johannesburg from July to November 2022 who had previously been part of ADVANCE and were not pregnant at the time of screening. Participants switching either TAF/FTC + DTG or TDF/FTC/EFV to TDF/3TC/DTG showed statistically significant reductions in weight, low-density lipoprotein, triglycerides, glucose and glycated hemoglobin.",The paper does not mention any publicly available sequences as it does not report on HIV sequences.
36519389,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No GenBank accession numbers,This study did not report HIV sequences from patient samples or genbank accession,The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers as it does not report on HIV sequences.
36519389,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,0,"CHARACTERISE enrolled residents of inner-city Johannesburg from July to November 2022 who had previously been part of ADVANCE and were not pregnant at the time of screening. Participants switching either TAF/FTC + DTG or TDF/FTC/EFV to TDF/3TC/DTG showed statistically significant reductions in weight, low-density lipoprotein, triglycerides, glucose and glycated hemoglobin.",The paper does not report any individuals from whom samples were obtained for HIV sequencing.
