36645792,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa.  Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive HIV-1 RNA ≥1000 copies/mL) on first-line TEE.","The study involved patients with virologic failure on a first-line regimen and mentioned the collection of samples for genotypic antiretroviral resistance testing, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
36645792,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Our findings do not support the need for initial dolutegravir dose adjustment in patients switching to TLD who failed first-line TEE.  We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa. Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) RNA ≥1000 copies/mL 2–24 months apart) on a first-line regimen of tenofovir, emtricitabine (or lamivudine), and efavirenz. Exclusion criteria were CD4+ cell count <100 cells/µL; estimated glomerular filtration rate <50 mL/minute/1.73 m2; alanine aminotransferase >100 IU/L; total bilirubin more than twice the upper limit of normal; active opportunistic infection; active malignancy; pregnant or intention to become pregnant; breastfeeding; active psychiatric condition or substance abuse judged likely to impact adherence; and allergy or intolerance to one of the study drugs. Women of childbearing potential were required to receive effective contraception. On 14 July 2021, the study protocol was amended to include patients with CD4+ cell counts of between 50 and 100 cells/µL to facilitate recruitment.",The paper focuses on a clinical trial involving resistance testing but does not mention the collection of in vitro drug susceptibility data.
36645792,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"In Khayelitsha, 130 adults with virologic failure on first-line TEE were randomly assigned to switch to TLD with an initial lead-in dose of DTG or placebo in a 1:1 manner.  We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa. Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) RNA ≥1000 copies/mL 2–24 months apart) on a first-line regimen of tenofovir, emtricitabine (or lamivudine), and efavirenz. Theft     heroin. Clinically significant insomnia (ISI score ≥8) has been defined as “insomnia that causes distress or impairment in social, occupational or other important areas of functioning.”)  We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa. Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) RNA ≥1000 copies/mL 2–24 months apart) on a first-line regimen of tenofovir, emtricitabine (or lamivudine), and efavirenz. One participant met protocol-defined criteria for loss to follow-up before week 24 but returned at week 24 and had HIV-1 RNA level ≥1000 copies/mL. In Khayelitsha, 130 adults with virologic failure on first-line TEE were randomly assigned to switch to TLD with an initial lead-in dose of DTG or placebo in a 1:1 manner.  We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa. Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) RNA ≥1000 copies/mL 2–24 months apart) on a first-line regimen of tenofovir, emtricitabine (or lamivudine), and efavirenz. Baseline GART was performed retrospectively for all participants after completion of week 24 visits, on plasma samples stored at enrollment (with results not returned to clinicians).  In Khayelitsha, 130 adults with virologic failure on first-line TEE were randomly assigned to switch to TLD with an initial lead-in dose of DTG or placebo in a 1:1 manner. We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa. Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) RNA ≥1000 copies/mL 2–24 months apart) on a first-line regimen of tenofovir, emtricitabine (or lamivudine), and efavirenz.","The paper does not mention any publicly available sequences, indicating that the sequences were not made publicly available."
36645792,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates.,"We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa. Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) RNA ≥1000 copies/mL 2–24 months apart) on a first-line regimen of tenofovir, emtricitabine (or lamivudine), and efavirenz. Baseline GART was performed retrospectively for all participants after completion of week 24 visits, on plasma samples stored at enrollment (with results not returned to clinicians).",The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
36645792,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,130,"In Khayelitsha, 130 adults with virologic failure on first-line TEE were randomly assigned to switch to TLD with an initial lead-in dose of DTG or placebo in a 1:1 manner. We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa. Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) RNA ≥1000 copies/mL 2–24 months apart) on a first-line regimen of tenofovir, emtricitabine (or lamivudine), and efavirenz.  The majority (76%) of the 120 participants with successful baseline GART had mutations associated with at least low-level resistance to both tenofovir and lamivudine","The paper states that 130 participants were randomized in the study, which implies that samples were obtained from 130 individuals for HIV sequencing."
36645792,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,South Africa,"We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial in Khayelitsha, South Africa. Eligible patients had virologic failure (2 consecutive human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) RNA ≥1000 copies/mL 2–24 months apart) on a first-line regimen of tenofovir, emtricitabine (or lamivudine), and efavirenz.","The study was conducted in Khayelitsha, South Africa, indicating that the sequenced samples were obtained from South Africa."
