36660819,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"Overall, 12 of 522 (2.3%) participants in the Q8W arm and 2 of 523 (0.4%) in the Q4W arm had CVF, the study collected sample from virological failure.","The paper mentions that sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure, indicating that some participants experienced virological failure while on the treatment regimen."
36660819,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"The ATLAS-2M study was conducted following the Declaration of Helsinki. ATLAS-2M is a phase 3b, randomized, open-label, active-controlled, multicenter, parallel-group noninferiority study to evaluate the efficacy, safety, and tolerability of CAB+RPV LA administered Q8W versus Q4W in virologically suppressed PWH.","The paper describes the ATLAS-2M study as a phase 3b, randomized, open-label clinical trial, indicating that the patients were part of a clinical trial."
36660819,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"Here, we report the antiretroviral therapy as long acting suppression (ATLAS)-2M study week 152 results. ATLAS-2M is a phase 3b, randomized, multicenter study assessing the efficacy and safety of CAB+RPV LA every 8 weeks (Q8W) versus every 4 weeks (Q4W).","The paper does not mention any specific sequencing of HIV from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs, as no samples were obtained for sequencing."
