36660819,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,No samples were sequenced.,"Here, we report the antiretroviral therapy as long acting suppression (ATLAS)-2M study week 152 results. ATLAS-2M is a phase 3b, randomized, multicenter study assessing the efficacy and safety of CAB+RPV LA every 8 weeks (Q8W) versus every 4 weeks (Q4W).","The paper does not mention any specific drugs that were received by individuals before sequencing, as no samples were obtained for sequencing."
36694270,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"The matched CSF and plasma samples of 62 HIV-1 patients were tested at one study site in China (Chongqing; 2019--2022). CSF and matched plasma HIV-1 subtypes were confirmed in 62 patients, and the most frequent recombinant form was CRF07-BC (64.5%).",The paper mentions that matched CSF and plasma samples from 62 HIV-1 patients were tested for drug resistance and genotyping.
36694270,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"The aim of this study is to evaluate common HIV-1 resistance in CSF and compare it with resistance in matched plasma, and analyse the influencing factors of cerebrospinal fluid drug resistance. The matched CSF and plasma samples of 62 HIV-1 patients were tested at one study site in China (Chongqing; 2019–2022). HIV genotyping and drug resistance was evaluated using the Stanford v8.7 algorithm. The diagnosis and treatment data and basic information were collected from the clinical case system, and the influencing factors of drug resistance mutations in CSF was obtained by variance analysis. CSF and matched plasma HIV-1 subtypes were confirmed in 62 patients, and the most frequent recombinant form was CRF07-BC (64.5%). Thirteen patients (21.0%) were detected with drug-resistant mutations, and the sites were consistent in both CSF and matched plasma. The drug-resistant ratios of untreated patients and treated patients were 5/51 (9.8%) and 8/11 (72.7%), respectively. The type with the highest mutation frequency was NNRTI, and no mutation was found in INSTI. Multivariate analysis indicated that ARV treatment was associated with CSF resistance (P< 0.001). The subtypes and drug resistance mutation sites are consistent in CSF and matched plasma samples of HIV-1 patients, and there is a correlation between ARV treatment and possible drug resistance, especially in CSF reservoirs. These findings highlight the concern about CSF drug resistance in HIV patients.",The paper focuses on the genotypic analysis of drug resistance mutations in clinical samples and does not mention any in vitro testing of drug susceptibility.
36694270,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,"Sequences were then spliced and edited using the Seqman pro and Megalign7.0V software, and were submitted to the drug resistance database of Stanford University (https://hivdb.stanford.edu/hivdb/by-sequences/) for HIV-1 subtypes and resistance mutation analysis.","The paper mentions that sequences were submitted to the drug resistance database of Stanford University, indicating they were made publicly available."
36694270,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates are OQ325553 to OQ325614.,All sequences have been submitted to GenBank (accession numbers OQ325553 to OQ325614).,The paper explicitly lists the GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
36694270,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,62,"As a result, a total of 62 patients were included in this study, and all test reports were recorded.",The paper states that a total of 62 patients were included in the study after testing for drug resistance.
36694270,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,China,The matched CSF and plasma samples of 62 HIV-1 patients were tested at one study site in China (Chongqing; 2019–2022).,The paper specifies that the study was conducted at one study site in China (Chongqing).
36694270,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2019-2022,"The matched CSF and plasma samples of 62 HIV-1 patients were tested at one study site in China (Chongqing; 2019–2022). We retrospectively collected matched pairs of 68 HIV-1 patients who were admitted to Chongqing Public Health Medical Center from June 2020 to June 2022 and completed plasma CD4+ T cell counts, HIV RNA viral load, and CSF biochemical tests.",The paper mentions that the samples were obtained between 2019 and 2022.
36694270,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"One-step RT-PCR and nested PCR was performed on a GeneAmp®9700PCR instrument (ABI, USA). The target bands were subjected to 1% agarose gel electrophoresis for validation, and the amplified product was sequenced. PCR primers are listed in Supplementary Table 1. We amplified the nucleotide sequences of HIV-1 protease, reverse transcriptase and integrase using nested polymerase chain reaction (nest-pcr) method. A viral nucleic acid extraction kit (Jiangsu Shuoshi Company, China) was used to extract RNA from 00 μL plasma and CFS.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing; it uses PCR methods for amplification and sequencing of the HIV-1 sequences directly from the clinical samples.
36694270,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"protease, reverse transcriptase, integrase","We amplified the nucleotide sequences of HIV-1 protease, reverse transcriptase and integrase using nested polymerase chain reaction (nest-pcr) method.","The paper specifically mentions that the nucleotide sequences of the HIV-1 protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes were amplified and sequenced."
36694270,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"One-step RT-PCR and nested PCR was performed on a GeneAmp®9700PCR instrument (ABI, USA). The target bands were subjected to 1% agarose gel electrophoresis for validation, and the amplified product was sequenced.","The paper describes the use of PCR followed by gel electrophoresis to validate the products, which indicates Sanger sequencing was used."
36694270,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,CSF and plasma samples,The matched CSF and plasma samples of 62 HIV-1 patients were tested at one study site in China (Chongqing; 2019–2022). CSF and plasma samples were tested for drug resistance of HIV genotypes.,The paper mentions that matched CSF and plasma samples were used for the study.
36694270,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"Among the 13 patients with resistance mutation sites, the CSF and plasma subtypes were identical, mainly CRF07-BC (n = 5), and the mutation sites were consistent, and most of the patient had more than one mutation site. The median CD4 cell count values (IQR) in non-treated and treated patients were 61 (35–106) and 76 (23–136) cells/mm3, respectively.","The paper mentions that some patients had developed resistance mutations, which indicates they experienced virological failure."
36694270,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"We retrospectively collected matched pairs of 68 HIV-1 patients who were admitted to Chongqing Public Health Medical Center from June 2020 to June 2022 and completed plasma CD4+ T cell counts, HIV RNA viral load, and CSF biochemical tests.",The paper does not indicate that the patients were part of a clinical trial; it mentions a retrospective collection of data from patients admitted to a medical center.
