36751650,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"Individuals newly diagnosed with HIV in Guangxi from 2016 to 2020, which mainly included MSM and the heterosexual (HES) population, were recruited in this study. These individuals must meet the following requirements: (1) newly diagnosed with HIV-1; (2) had not received ART; (3) followed the informed consent of participants. Peripheral blood samples and epidemiological data were also collected. Plasma was separated within 12 hours of blood collection and stored at −80°C until further use. CD4+ T-cell count and viral load are the main indicators of treatment effect in the study. Blood samples were collected for CD4+ T-cell counts and viral load before ART.","The paper mentioned that they recruited ' newly diagnosed with HIV' individuals and who 'had not received ART', which means they had not received ARV drugs."
36779485,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,We investigated rilpivirine cross-resistance in treatment-naive and experienced patients in South Africa. Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described.,"The paper discusses the analysis of genotypic sequence data from patients, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
36779485,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Baseline rilpivirine drug resistance mutations (DRMs) are a risk factor for virological failure in patients treated with long-acting cabotegravir and rilpivirine (CAB/RPV LA). We investigated rilpivirine cross-resistance in treatment-naive and experienced patients in South Africa. One in 10 treatment-naive patients and 74.5% of patients failing treatment presented with rilpivirine DRMs. Our data suggest targeted genotyping may be required for patients initiating CAB/RPV LA, which significantly complicates the currently used public health approach.","The paper focuses on drug resistance mutations and their prevalence in patients, but it does not mention any in vitro susceptibility testing of drugs on viral isolates from patients. This indicates that the study is more clinical and observational rather than a laboratory-based susceptibility study, which would involve testing drug concentrations against viral replication in vitro. These sentences shows that the paper is focusing on the genotypic resistance data from patient samples rather than in vitro susceptibity data. In vitro da. Therefore, No is the answer."
36779485,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described. Pol sequences were submitted to Stanford HIVdb v9.0 to identify rilpivirine DRMs.,"The paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available. It only states that the sequences were submitted to Stanford HIVdb v9.0 for analysis, which does not constitute public availability in a database such as GenBank. This indicates that while the sequences were used for analysis, they were not archived in a publicly accessible database."
36779485,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No accession numbers were provided,We investigated rilpivirine cross-resistance in treatment-naive and experienced patients in South Africa. Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described. Pol sequences were submitted to Stanford HIVdb v9.0 to identify rilpivirine DRMs.,"The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates. It only describes the submission of sequences to the Stanford HIVdb v9.0 tool for analysis, which does not involve assigning GenBank accession numbers. Therefore, no accession numbers were provided."
36779485,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,1649,Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described.,"The paper states that genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis. Adding these two groups together, a total of 1649 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing."
36779485,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,South Africa,"We investigated rilpivirine cross-resistance in treatment-naive and experienced patients in South Africa. CAB/RPV LA treatment, with its potential to improve treatment adherence and reduce stigma among other advantages, is a promising addition to the available treatment arsenal . However, this regimen is recommended in virologically suppressed patients without treatment failure or suspected resistance, with the exception of isolated K103N.","The paper specifies that the study was conducted on patients in South Africa, indicating that all sequenced samples were obtained from this country."
36779485,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,Not provided,"Patients initiating ART (n=277) had a median age of 34 years (interquartile range (IQR): 291). Most were women (58.8%). Two patients (0.6%) presented with a subtype A recombinant virus. At least one NNRTI DRM was detected in 47 patients (17.0%), of whom 34 (12.3%) presented with at least one rilpivirine DRM. Twenty-seven ART initiators (9.7%) presented with predicted intermediate rilpivirine resistance, most often caused by E138A/G (n=20) and six (2.2%) presented with high-level resistance to rilpivirine, including four with at least two rilpivirine DRMs. Patients failing NNRTI-based ART (n=1372) were mostly women (63.6%) with a median age of 37 years (interquartile range: 311). Eight patients (0.8%) presented with a subtype A or subtype A recombinant virus. Almost all patients experiencing treatment failure (n=1305; 95.1%) presented with at least one NNRTI DRM, including 1022 (74.5%) with at least one rilpivirine DRM and 516 (37.6%) with at least two rilpivirine DRMs. Prevalence of rilpivirine DRMs is presented in Fig. 1. Almost three-quarters of patients showed intermediate (28.1%; n=385) and high-level rilpivirine resistance (44.3%; n=608)","The paper does not provide specific years during which the samples were obtained. It mentions the study was about the recent treatment initiated patients and most of the patients were experienced with non RNRTI, it was focusing on a recently developed regimen, which is cabotegravir and rilpivirine, so the treatmnt started which means all the samples were in a recent year. But the exact years are not mention in the paper."
36779485,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,Not provided,Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described. Pol sequences were submitted to Stanford HIVdb v9.0 to identify rilpivirine DRMs.,The paper does not mention whether the samples were cloned prior to sequencing. It only describes the use of genotypic sequence data from patient samples.
36779485,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Pol,Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described. Pol sequences were submitted to Stanford HIVdb v9.0 to identify rilpivirine DRMs.,"The paper specifies that Pol sequences were submitted to Stanford HIVdb v9.0 to identify rilpivirine DRMs, indicating that the Pol gene was sequenced."
36779485,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Not provided,Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described. Pol sequences were submitted to Stanford HIVdb v9.0 to identify rilpivirine DRMs.,The paper does not provide specific details on the sequencing method used. It only describes the analysis of genotypic sequence data.
36779485,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Not provided,"Baseline rilpivirine drug resistance mutations (DRMs) are a risk factor for virological failure in patients treated with long-acting cabotegravir and rilpivirine (CAB/RPV LA). We investigated rilpivirine cross-resistance in treatment-naive and experienced patients in South Africa. Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described. Pol sequences were submitted to Stanford HIVdb v9.0 to identify rilpivirine DRMs. The following mutations were included as rilpivirine DRMs (Stanford HIVdb penalty score ≥10): A98G, V100IV, K101EPH, V106I, E138AGKQR, V179DEFL, Y181CFGISV, Y188FL, G190ACEQSTV, H221Y, F227C, and 230IL.","The paper does not specify the type of clinical specimens sequenced, focusing on the analysis of genetic data from patient samples."
36779485,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,We investigated rilpivirine cross-resistance in treatment-naive and experienced patients in South Africa. Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described. Almost all patients experiencing treatment failure (n=1305; 95.1%) presented with at least one NNRTI DRM.,"The paper mentions the sequences were obtained from 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure, indicating that some sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure."
36779485,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"Screening for existing DRMs is logistically and technically challenging in LMICs and could be a barrier to use of CAB/RPV LA. This analysis indicates that rilpivirine DRMs are common in a setting wherein NNRTI-based treatment was recently widely implemented, and has significant implications for operational implementation of CAB/RPV LA.",The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial; it focuses on the analysis of data from routine 223790626 treatment initiation and failure 5 8 1 1. The fact that the paper mention the the challage for using the drug regimen in a low income country also indicates that the study is not from a clinical trial.
36779485,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,We investigated rilpivirine cross-resistance in treatment-naive and experienced patients in South Africa. Genotypic sequence data from 277 patients initiating ART and 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure were included for analysis as previously described. Almost all patients experiencing treatment failure (n=1305; 95.1%) presented with at least one NNRTI DRM. Patients failing NNRTI-based ART (n=1372) were mostly women (63.6%) with a median age of 37 years (interquartile range: 31--42).,"The paper mentions the sequences were from 1372 patients experiencing NNRTI-treatment failure, which means they had previously received ARV drugs."
36779485,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI,NNRTI","Patients initiating ART (n = 277) had a median age of 34 years (interquartile range (IQR): 29--42) and most were women (58.8%). Two patients (0.6%) presented with a subtype A recombinant virus. At least one NNRTI DRM was detected in 47 patients (17.0%), of whom 34 (12.3%) presented with at least one rilpivirine DRM. Twenty-seven ART initiators (9.7%) presented with predicted intermediate rilpivirine resistance, most often caused by E138A/G (n = 20) and six (2.2%) presented with high-level resistance to rilpivirine, including four with at least two rilpivirine DRMs. Patients failing NNRTI-based ART (n = 1372) were mostly women (63.6%) with a median age of 37 years (interquartile range: 31--42). Eight patients (0.8%) presented with a subtype A or subtype A recombinant virus. Almost all patients experiencing treatment failure (n = 1305; 95.1%) presented with at least one NNRTI DRM, including 1022 (74.5%) with at least one rilpivirine DRM and 516 (37.6%) with at least two rilpivirine DRMs. Prevalence of rilpivirine DRMs is presented in Fig. 1. Almost three-quarters of patients showed intermediate (28.1%; n = 385) and high-level rilpivirine resistance (44.3%; n = 608).","The paper mentions that patients were receiving NNRTI-based ART, and also mention the fact that the patienrs were initiating ART, which means all the patients received NRTI and some also received integrase inhibitors because the drug cabotegravir was used, but the exact sequence of drugs and drug classes was not detailed."
36779485,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not provided,"Patients initiating ART (n = 277) had a median age of 34 years (interquartile range (IQR): 29--42) and most were women (58.8%). Two patients (0.6%) presented with a subtype A recombinant virus. At least one NNRTI DRM was detected in 47 patients (17.0%), of whom 34 (12.3%) presented with at least one rilpivirine DRM. Twenty-seven ART initiators (9.7%) presented with predicted intermediate rilpivirine resistance, most often caused by E138A/G (n = 20) and six (2.2%) presented with high-level resistance to rilpivirine, including four with at least two rilpivirine DRMs. Patients failing NNRTI-based ART (n = 1372) were mostly women (63.6%) with a median age of 37 years (interquartile range: 31--42). Eight patients (0.8%) presented with a subtype A or subtype A recombinant virus. Almost all patients experiencing treatment failure (n = 1305; 95.1%) presented with at least one NNRTI DRM, including 1022 (74.5%) with at least one rilpivirine DRM and 516 (37.6%) with at least two rilpivirine DRMs. Prevalence of rilpivirine DRMs is presented in Fig. 1. Almost three-quarters of patients showed intermediate (28.1%; n = 385) and high-level rilpivirine resistance (44.3%; n = 608)","The paper mentions that patients were receiving NNRTI-based ART, but it dosent mention the exact drugs the patients received before the sample sequencing."
36795586,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,We conducted a retrospective cohort study analyzing CALHIV of 0--19 years old and weighing greater than or equal to 20 kg who received DTG as part of their HIV care between January 2017 and December 2020. The cohort included new ART initiations using a DTG-based ART and ART-experienced patients who shifted to a DTG-based regimen (irrespective of virologic status).,"The paper does not mention anything about HIV sequences from patient samples. It focuses on the effectiveness and safety of dolutegravir in treating children and adolescents living with HIV, and does not discuss any sequencing of HIV samples from patients."
36795586,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,We conducted a retrospective cohort study analyzing CALHIV of 0--19 years old and weighing greater than or equal to 20 kg who received DTG as part of their HIV care between January 2017 and December 2020. The cohort included new ART initiations using a DTG-based ART and ART-experienced patients who shifted to a DTG-based regimen (irrespective of virologic status). Gathering of ARV drug resistance mutations via HIV Genotype testing was not available as part of routine care at the COE or pre-switch to DTG.,"The paper does not report any in vitro drug susceptibility data. It mainly discusses the clinical outcomes of dolutegravir treatment in children and adolescents living with HIV, including effectiveness and safety, but does not include any laboratory-based drug susceptibility testing data."
