36961945,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"Plasma HIV RNA levels were measured at baseline (Day 0), weeks 2, 4, 8, 12, 24, 36, 48, and every 24 weeks thereafter Viral rebound was defined as a single viral load >50 copies/mL after an undetectable level as previously described. No participants experienced virologic failure after initiating ART during the median 25.39 ± 3.13 months of follow-up on treatment.","The paper mentions that plasma HIV RNA levels were measured and defines viral rebound, which indicates monitoring of virological failure. However, it states that no participants experienced virologic failure after initiating ART."
