mutations in reverse transcriptase","The evidence specifies the NRTIs and NNRTIs that were administered to patients, categorizing them into first, second, and mixed-generation regimens."
37515095,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"3TC, ABC, AZT, D4T, DDI, FTC, TDF, ETR, EFV, NVP, RPV, DRV/r, LPV/r","Individual ART regimens were summarized as 1st-, 2nd-, or mixed-generation regimens according to the specific nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs) and non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs) administered: zidovudine (AZT), didanosine (DDI), stavudine (D4T), and lamivudine (3TC) were classified as 1st-generation NRTIs; abacavir (ABC), tenofovir (TDF), and emtricitabine (FTC) were classified as 2nd-generation NRTIs; nevirapine (NVP) was classified as a 1st-generation NNRTI; and efavirenz (EFV), etravirine (ETR), and rilpivirine (RPV) were classified as 2nd-generation NNRTIs. Any protease inhibitors (PIs, darunavir/ritonavir, DRV/r; DRV/cobicistat, DRV/c; lopinavir/r, LPV/r) or integrase strand transfer inhibitors (INSTIs, dolutegravir, DTG) administered were not considered for the 1st-, 2nd-, or mixed-generation regimen classification, as subsequent analysis of DRMs only considered mutations in reverse transcriptase Individual ART regimens were summarized as 1st-, 2nd-, or mixed-generation regimens according to the specific nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs) and non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs) administered: zidovudine (AZT), didanosine (DDI), stavudine (D4T), and lamivudine (3TC) were classified as 1st-generation NRTIs; abacavir (ABC), tenofovir (TDF), and emtricitabine (FTC) were classified as 2nd-generation NRTIs; nevirapine (NVP) was classified as a 1st-generation NNRTI; and efavirenz (EFV), etravirine (ETR), and rilpivirine (RPV) were classified as 2nd-generation NNRTIs. Any protease inhibitors (PIs, darunavir/ritonavir, DRV/r; DRV/cobicistat, DRV/c; lopinavir/r, LPV/r) or integrase strand transfer inhibitors (INSTIs, dolutegravir, DTG) administered were not considered for the 1st-, 2nd-, or mixed-generation regimen classification, as subsequent analysis of DRMs only considered mutations in reverse transcriptase. Ove 1/355 (85.6%) participants had sequences resistant to at least one drug on their ART regimen.","The evidence lists the specific drugs that were administered to individuals in the study, indicating that these drugs were received prior to sequencing."
37515146,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"In total, 379 sequences were obtained from participants (62% female, mean age 36 ± 10 years).; A total of 391 participants were recruited, with sequencing successfully carried out in 379 individual participant samples, giving a genotyping success rate of 96.9%.","The paper reports that HIV-1 pre-treatment drug resistance (PDR) patterns were described based on sequences obtained from participants in Cameroon. Specifically, it mentions that 379 sequences were obtained from participants, indicating that the study involved HIV sequences from patient samples."
37515146,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"We described HIV-1 pre-treatment drug resistance (PDR) patterns, effect of viral clades on PDR, and programmatic implications on first-line regimens in Cameroon. A sentinel surveillance of PDR was conducted from 2014 to 2019. Sequencing of HIV-1 protease and reverse transcriptase was performed, and HIVDR was interpreted using Stanford HIVdb.v.9.4. In total, 379 sequences were obtained from participants (62% female, mean age 36 ± 10 years). The overall PDR rate was 15.0% [95% CI: 11.8--19.0] nationwide, with significant disparity between regions (p = 0.03).",The paper focuses on pre-treatment drug resistance (PDR) patterns and genotypic resistance testing using sequences obtained from patient samples. It does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility assays or data.
37515146,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,"Sequence data are available on GenBank under the accession numbers GenBank MK702015-MK702057, MK867695-MK867757, and MK995397-MK995457.","The paper explicitly states that sequence data are available on GenBank under the specified accession numbers, indicating that the sequences have been made publicly available."
37515146,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,"GenBank MK702015-MK702057, MK867695-MK867757, and MK995397-MK995457","Sequence data are available on GenBank under the accession numbers GenBank MK702015-MK702057, MK867695-MK867757, and MK995397-MK995457.","The paper provides specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, confirming their availability in the database."
37515146,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,379,"In total, 379 sequences were obtained from participants (62% female, mean age 36 ± 10 years).; A total of 391 participants were recruited, with sequencing successfully carried out in 379 individual participant samples, giving a genotyping success rate of 96.9%.","The paper states that 379 sequences were obtained from participants, indicating that samples were successfully obtained for HIV sequencing from 379 individuals."
37515146,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Cameroon,"We described HIV-1 pre-treatment drug resistance (PDR) patterns, effect of viral clades on PDR, and programmatic implications on first-line regimens in Cameroon. A sentinel surveillance of PDR was conducted from 2014 to 2019. The enrollment of participants was carried out in health facilities of eight regions of Cameroon: Centre, Littoral, East, West, Northwest, Southwest, North, and Far North.",The paper focuses on HIV-1 pre-treatment drug resistance patterns in Cameroon and mentions that the enrollment of participants was carried out in health facilities across eight regions of Cameroon.
37515146,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2014 to 2019,"We carried out a cross-sectional and analytical study for five years, from December 2014 to June 2019. A sentinel surveillance of PDR was conducted from 2014 to 2019.","The paper states that the study was conducted from 2014 to 2019, indicating the time frame during which the sequenced samples were obtained."
37515146,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"Sequencing of HIV-1 protease and reverse transcriptase was performed, and HIVDR was interpreted using Stanford HIVdb.v.9.4. Genotypic resistance testing was carried out in the pol gene (reverse transcriptase and protease regions) as follows. For the amplification of the pol region, a previously validated inhouse genotyping assay was used. The PCR products were revealed using 1% agarose gel electrophoresis. The sequencing reaction obtained were purified by exclusion chromatography on SEPHADEX G50 resin and then sequenced using a genetic analyzer (ABI 3500®).","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It describes direct sequencing of PCR products, which means cloning was not necessary."
37515146,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Protease and reverse transcriptase,"Sequencing of HIV-1 protease and reverse transcriptase was performed, and HIVDR was interpreted using Stanford HIVdb.v.9.4. Genotypic resistance testing was carried out in the pol gene (reverse transcriptase and protease regions) as follows.","The paper reports sequencing of the HIV-1 protease and reverse transcriptase regions, which are part of the pol gene."
37515146,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,The PCR products were revealed using 1% agarose gel electrophoresis. The sequencing reaction obtained were purified by exclusion chromatography on SEPHADEX G50 resin and then sequenced using a genetic analyzer (ABI 3500®).,"The paper describes the use of a genetic analyzer (ABI 3500) for sequencing, which is indicative of Sanger sequencing."
37515146,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"For each participant, 10 mL of venous blood was collected in an EDTA tube. The tubes were centrifuged at a speed of 1800 rpm, separated for plasma collection, plasma aliquoted (1 mL) in cryotubes, stored at -20 °C, and transported to the CIRCB, where biological analyzes were carried out.","The paper mentions that plasma was collected and sequenced, indicating that plasma samples were used for the HIV sequencing."
37515146,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"Included in our study were HIV-1 infected patients aged above 19 years (adults per WHO definitions) with no prior history of ART treatment. At the regional level, we observed a significant disparity between the values of the global resistance threshold, ranging from 9.8% in the North region to 27.5% in the Far North region, *p* = 0.03.","The paper included treatment-naïve individuals, so no sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen."
37515146,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"We carried out a cross-sectional and analytical study for five years, from December 2014 to June 2019. The enrollment of participants was carried out in health facilities of eight regions of Cameroon: Centre, Littoral, East, West, Northwest, Southwest, North, and Far North. The study participants consisted of adult patients initiating ART in the health facilities of regions previously cited. Patients presenting for ART initiation at the various recruitment sites were encountered by the recruitment clinician.","The paper describes a cross-sectional and analytical study, not a clinical trial, indicating that the patients were not part of a trial."
37515146,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"Included in our study were HIV-1 infected patients aged above 19 years (adults per WHO definitions) with no prior history of ART treatment. Two regions had EFV/NVP PDR above the 10% critical threshold, namely the Far North (15%) and East (10.9%).","The paper included treatment-naïve individuals, so no sequences were obtained from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
37515146,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"Included in our study were HIV-1 infected patients aged above 19 years (adults per WHO definitions) with no prior history of ART treatment. Patients presenting for ART initiation at the various recruitment sites were encountered by the recruitment clinician. Antiretroviral treatment (ART) initiation in health facilities of the eight regions of Cameroon. The 379 participants with successful sequencing data were from eight regions distributed as follows: 53 (14%) from the Center, 40 (10.6%) for the Far North, 46 (12.1%) for the East, 41 (10.8%) for the Littoral, 44 (11.6%) for the North, 61 (16.1%) for the Northwest, 49 (12.9%) for the West and 45 (11.9%) for the Southwest. The morality rate on study shows 80% of participants not on Azidothymidine, 72% not on Lamivudine, 71% not on Tenofovir, 76% not on Nevirapine, 72% not Efavirenz, 80% not on Lopinavir/Ritonavir, 80% Not on Raltegravir, 69% on other drugs. The majority of participants were female (62%), with ages ranging from 20 to 80 years and a mean ± SD of 36 ± 10 years.","The paper included treatment-naïve individuals, so no sequences were obtained from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
37515146,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"Included in our study were HIV-1 infected patients aged above 19 years (adults per WHO definitions) with no prior history of ART treatment. Patients presenting for ART initiation at the various recruitment sites were encountered by the recruitment clinician. Antiretroviral treatment (ART) initiation in health facilities of the eight regions of Cameroon. The 379 participants with successful sequencing data were from eight regions distributed as follows: 53 (14%) from the Center, 40 (10.6%) for the Far North, 46 (12.1%) for the East, 41 (10.8%) for the Littoral, 44 (11.6%) for the North, 61 (16.1%) for the Northwest, 49 (12.9%) for the West and 45 (11.9%) for the Southwest. The morality rate on study shows 80% of participants not on Azidothymidine, 72% not on Lamivudine, 71% not on Tenofovir, 76% not on Nevirapine, 72% not Efavirenz, 80% not on Lopinavir/Ritonavir, 80% Not on Raltegravir, 69% on other drugs. The majority of participants were female (62%), with ages ranging from 20 to 80 years and a mean ± SD of 36 ± 10 years.","The paper included treatment-naïve individuals, so no sequences were obtained from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
37520425,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"HIV-1 genotypic resistance testing (GRT) before ART initiation was done in 14 of 30 viremic participants on DTG, among whom nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI), NNRTI, and protease inhibitors resistance was detected in 0 (0%), 2 (14%) and 1 (7%), respectively. No resistance was found in the 2 of 30 participants with available GRT at the time of viremia ≥50 copies/mL.","The paper mentions HIV-1 genotypic resistance testing (GRT) before ART initiation for 14 of 30 viremic participants on dolutegravir (DTG) and also GRT was done in 30 participants on DTG with viremia, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
37520425,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"We compared virological suppression at 12 months, after treatment initiation in the two cohorts of participants aged ≥15 years, initiating DTG- and NNRTI-based ART. Drug resistance was assessed among participants with viremia ≥50 copies/mL on DTG. Results Virological suppression was achieved for 165/195 (85%) and 154/211 (73) participants in the DTG- and NNRTI- cohorts, respectively ( P = 0.003). DTG-based ART was associated with >2 times the odds of viral suppression versus NNRTI-based ART (adjusted odds ratio, 2.10 [95% confidence interval {CI}, 1.12--3.94]; adjusted risk ratio, 1.11 [95% CI, 1.00--1.24]). HIV-1 genotypic resistance testing (GRT) before ART initiation was done in 14 of 30 viremic participants on DTG, among whom nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI), NNRTI, and protease inhibitors resistance was detected in 0 (0%), 2 (14%) and 1 (7%), respectively. No resistance was found in the 2 of 30 participants with available GRT at the time of viremia ≥50 copies/mL.","The paper discusses virological suppression and genotypic resistance testing in patients, focusing on the presence of drug resistance mutations, but it does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data."
37520425,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,"For this study, we performed HIV-1 genotypic resistance testing (GRT) from biobanked samples for those with an HIV VL ≥50 copies/mL. In addition, HIV-1 GRT was performed on samples available prior to treatment initiation for cases with a VL ≥50 copies/mL at 12 months using cryopreserved samples, to determine PDR before ART initiation in the DTG cohort. GRT was performed using a validated in-house polymerase chain reaction (PCR) protocol to determine the HIV-1 drug resistance--associated mutations for reverse transcriptase, protease, and INSTI [16, 17]. In brief, RNA was extracted from 150 μL of plasma using the PureLink Viral RNA/DNA Mini Kit (Invitrogen, Thermo Fisher Scientific), according to the manufacturer's protocol. RNA extracts were retrotranscribed and amplified using the HIV-1 Genotyping Kit Amplification Module (Applied Biosystems, Thermo Fisher Scientific). A direct sequencing reaction was done using 6 overlapping primers, and assembly program (BioEdit 7.2) was used for sequence analysis. Mutations were interpreted according to the Stanford University's HIV Drug Resistance Database Program version 9.2 (http://hivdb.stanford.edu). Drug resistance mutations conferring low, intermediate, or high-level resistance were considered. The reported protease and reverse transcriptase sequences are available in GenBank (accession number OQ627458-OQ627474).","The paper mentions that the sequences are available in GenBank under the accession numbers OQ627458-OQ627474, indicating that they were made publicly available."
37520425,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,OQ627458-OQ627474,The reported protease and reverse transcriptase sequences are available in GenBank (accession number OQ627458-OQ627474).,The paper explicitly states that the protease and reverse transcriptase sequences are available in GenBank under the accession numbers OQ627458-OQ627474.
37520425,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,30,"HIV-1 genotypic resistance testing (GRT) before ART initiation was done in 14 of 30 viremic participants on DTG, among whom nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI), NNRTI, and protease inhibitors resistance was detected in 0 (0%), 2 (14%) and 1 (7%), respectively. For patients with viremia at 12 months after starting DTG-based ART, blood plasma samples prior to treatment initiation were available for 25 of 30 (83%) patients.","Paper mentioned blood plasma samples prior to treatment initiation were available for 25 of 30 patients, in which 14 of 25 were able to do GRT before ART initiation, this means 30 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing."
37520425,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Tanzania,"This is a retrospective, observational study nested within the Kilombero and Ulanga antiretroviral cohort (KIULARCO), a prospective cohort of PWH. The cohort includes patients seen at the Chronic Diseases Clinic of Ifakara, the care and treatment center for PWH of the Saint Francis Referral Hospital, located in rural southeastern Tanzania.","Paper mentioned this study is conducted in Tanzania, and all of the patients have been seen at the Saint Francis Referral Hospital in Tanzania."
37520425,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2016-2020,"This is a retrospective, observational study nested within the Kilombero and Ulanga antiretroviral cohort (KIULARCO), a prospective cohort of PWH. Two groups of PWH aged ≥15 years attending KIULARCO were included in the analysis: (1) treatment-naive patients initiating NNRTI-based ART between 16 December 2016 and 15 December 2017 (referred to as the NNRTI cohort) and (2) treatment-naive patients initiating DTG-based ART between 16 March 2019 and 15 September 2020 (referred to as the DTG cohort).",The paper mentions that the samples were obtained from patients initiating NNRTI-based ART between December 2016 and December 2017 and DTG-based ART between March 2019 and September 2020.
37520425,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"GRT was performed using a validated in-house polymerase chain reaction (PCR) protocol to determine the HIV-1 drug resistance--associated mutations for reverse transcriptase, protease, and INSTI [16, 17]. In brief, RNA was extracted from 150 μL of plasma using the PureLink Viral RNA/DNA Mini Kit (Invitrogen, Thermo Fisher Scientific), according to the manufacturer's protocol. RNA extracts were retrotranscribed and amplified using the HIV-1 Genotyping Kit Amplification Module (Applied Biosystems, Thermo Fisher Scientific). A direct sequencing reaction was done using 6 overlapping primers, and assembly program (BioEdit 7.2) was used for sequence analysis. Mutations were interpreted according to the Stanford University’s HIV Drug Resistance Database Program version 9.2 (http://hivdb.stanford.edu).","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It describes direct sequencing of PCR products, which indicates that cloning was not performed."
37520425,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"Protease, Reverse Transcriptase, Integrase","GRT was performed using a validated in-house polymerase chain reaction (PCR) protocol to determine the HIV-1 drug resistance--associated mutations for reverse transcriptase, protease, and INSTI [16, 17].","The paper mentions the sequencing of drug resistance-associated mutations for reverse transcriptase, protease, and integrase, indicating that these genes were sequenced."
37520425,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"A direct sequencing reaction was done using 6 overlapping primers, and assembly program (BioEdit 7.2) was used for sequence analysis. Mutations were interpreted according to the Stanford University's HIV Drug Resistance Database Program version 9.2 (http://hivdb.stanford.edu).","The paper describes the use of overlapping primers and direct sequencing followed by assembly program and analysis using BioEdit 7.2, which is consistent with Sanger sequencing method."
37520425,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"RNA was extracted from 150 μL of plasma using the PureLink Viral RNA/DNA Mini Kit (Invitrogen, Thermo Fisher Scientific), according to the manufacturer's protocol. VL measurement was done using the Abbott Real-time m2000 HIV-1 Assay (Abbott Laboratories, Chicago, Illinois), with a reportable range of 40--10 000 000 copies/mL for blood plasma. Blood plasma samples at VL ≥50 copies/mL were available for 13 of 30 (43%) patients.",The paper mentions that RNA was extracted from plasma and VL measurement was done using plasma.
37520425,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"No resistance was found in the 2 of 30 participants with available GRT at the time of viremia ≥50 copies/mL. HIV-1 genotypic resistance testing (GRT) before ART initiation was done in 14 of 30 viremic participants on DTG, among whom nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI), NNRTI, and protease inhibitors resistance was detected in 0 (0%), 2 (14%) and 1 (7%), respectively. HIV-1 GRT was performed on samples available prior to treatment initiation for cases with a VL ≥50 copies/mL at 12 months using cryopreserved samples, to determine PDR before ART initiation in the DTG cohort. Blood plasma samples at VL ≥50 copies/mL were available for 13 of 30 (43%) patients. For patients with viremia at 12 months after starting DTG-based ART, blood plasma samples prior to treatment initiation were available for 25 of 30 (83%) patients. Among those with VL results available, viral suppression was achieved for 165 of 195 (85%) and 154 of 211 (73%) participants in the DTG and NNRTI cohorts, respectively ( P = .003).","The paper mentions that HIV-1 genotypic resistance testing (GRT) was performed on samples from participants with viremia ≥50 copies/mL on DTG and also mentions GRT was performed on samples available prior to treatment initiation for cases with a VL ≥50 copies/mL at 12 months using cryopreserved samples, to determine PDR, which means sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure."
37520425,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"This is a retrospective, observational study nested within the Kilombero and Ulanga antiretroviral cohort (KIULARCO), a prospective cohort of PWH. We compared virological suppression at 12 months, after treatment initiation in the two cohorts of participants aged ≥15 years, initiating DTG- and NNRTI-based ART. The cohort includes patients seen at the Chronic Diseases Clinic of Ifakara, the care and treatment center for PWH of the Saint Francis Referral Hospital, located in rural southeastern Tanzania.","The paper describes the study as a retrospective, observational study nested within a cohort, not a clinical trial."
37520425,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"We excluded patients initiating protease inhibitor (PI)--based therapy in both periods, patients starting NNRTI-based ART between 16 March 2019 and 15 September 2020, treatment-experienced patients (assessed in the baseline questionnaire by asking if they had ever received ART before),those not starting ART during the given time periods, and those without written informed consent to KIULARCO (Figure 1).","The paper was excluding treatment-experienced patients which means patients who had previously received ARV drugs. The cohort includes patients seen at the Chronic Diseases Clinic of Ifakara, the care and treatment center for PWH of the Saint Francis Referral Hospital, located in rural southeastern Tanzania. The cohort was established in 2005 and captures comprehensive demographic and clinical data, including ART use and monitoring, comorbidities, and treatment outcomes, with details described previously [14, 15]. Means the cohort has patients who had previously received ARV drugs."
37520425,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, INSTI","We compared virological suppression at 12 months, after treatment initiation in the two cohorts of participants aged ≥15 years, initiating DTG- and NNRTI-based ART. In addition, HIV-1 GRT was performed on samples available prior to treatment initiation for cases with a VL ≥50 copies/mL at 12 months using cryopreserved samples, to determine PDR before ART initiation in the DTG cohort. We excluded patients initiating protease inhibitor (PI)--based therapy in both periods, patients starting NNRTI-based ART between 16 March 2019 and 15 September 2020, treatment-experienced patients (assessed in the baseline questionnaire by asking if they had ever received ART before),those not starting ART during the given time periods, and those without written informed consent to KIULARCO (Figure 1),","The paper mentions that participants were receiving NNRTI-based or DTG-based regimens, and GRT was performed to determine PDR before ART initiation on samples available prior to treatment initiation, which indicates that drugs from the NRTI, NNRTI, and INSTI classes were received."
37520425,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, INSTI","We compared virological suppression at 12 months, after treatment initiation in the two cohorts of participants aged ≥15 years, initiating DTG- and NNRTI-based ART. In addition, HIV-1 GRT was performed on samples available prior to treatment initiation for cases with a VL ≥50 copies/mL at 12 months using cryopreserved samples, to determine PDR before ART initiation in the DTG cohort. We excluded patients initiating protease inhibitor (PI)--based therapy in both periods, patients starting NNRTI-based ART between 16 March 2019 and 15 September 2020, treatment-experienced patients (assessed in the baseline questionnaire by asking if they had ever received ART before),those not starting ART during the given time periods, and those without written informed consent to KIULARCO (Figure 1),","The paper mentions that participants were receiving NNRTI-based or DTG-based regimens, and GRT was performed to determine PDR before ART initiation on samples available prior to treatment initiation, which indicates that drugs from the NRTI, NNRTI, and INSTI classes were received."
37537871,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,77 plasma samples were subjected to HIV sequencing. These samples were collected from patients at Queen Mary Hospital in Hong Kong. The study describes the sequencing of HIV from these patient samples using various methods including Sanger sequencing and Illumina sequencing.,The paper mentions that 77 plasma samples from patients were collected and sequenced. This indicates that the HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples.
37537871,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,The paper discusses the sequencing and identification of drug resistance mutations in HIV quasispecies but does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility assays or data.,The focus of the paper is on sequencing and identifying drug resistance mutations rather than testing the susceptibility of the virus to drugs in vitro.
37537871,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,The paper does not mention that the sequences obtained from the study were deposited in a public database such as GenBank.,There is no information provided in the paper regarding the public availability of the sequences.
37537871,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No,The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates. There is no mention of the sequences being deposited in GenBank.,The paper does not include any information regarding the GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced isolates.
37537871,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,77,"A total of 77 plasma samples, collected from 70 male and 7 female patients ages 18 to 68, were obtained from the Queen Mary Hospital in Hong Kong.","The paper states that 77 plasma samples from 70 male and 7 female patients were collected, indicating that samples were obtained from 77 individuals."
37537871,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Hong Kong,The samples were collected from the Queen Mary Hospital in Hong Kong between 2002 and 2014.,"The paper clearly states that the samples were collected from Hong Kong, specifically from the Queen Mary Hospital."
37537871,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2002 to 2014,The samples were collected from the Queen Mary Hospital in Hong Kong between 2002 and 2014.,The paper mentions that the samples were collected over this period.
37537871,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It describes direct sequencing of RNA extracted from plasma samples.,The sequencing methods described do not involve cloning of the samples.
37537871,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"PR, RT, IN","Protease and reverse transcriptase nucleotide sequences were determined by our in-house Sanger sequencing-based genotypic resistance test, whereas the sequences of integrase were characterized by another in-house Sanger sequencing protocol developed by our team.","The paper mentions the sequencing of the protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes."
37537871,10,What method was used for sequencing?,"Sanger sequencing, Illumina sequencing, Nanopore sequencing","The study compares the results obtained from Sanger sequencing, Illumina sequencing, and ONT (Nanopore) sequencing in 77 HIV-positive plasma samples.","The paper describes the use of Sanger sequencing for protease and reverse transcriptase, Illumina sequencing for some samples, and Nano pore sequencing for the ONT workflow."
37537871,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples,77 plasma samples were collected from HIV-positive patients and subjected to various sequencing methods to evaluate drug resistance mutations.,The paper specifies that plasma samples were the clinical specimens sequenced in the study.
37537871,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"Long-Read Sequencing with Hierarchical Clustering for Antiretroviral Resistance Profiling of Mixed Human Immunodeficiency Virus Quasispecies. Results In the validation study, the abundance of detected quasispecies was concordant with the predicted result with the R2 of > 0.99. During the diagnostic evaluation, 59/77 samples were successfully sequenced for DRMs. Among 18 failed samples, 17 were below the limit of detection of 303.9 copies/μL. Based on the receiver operating characteristic analysis, the ONT workflow achieved an F1 score of 0.96 with a cutoff of 0.4 variant allele frequency. Four cases were found to have quasispecies with DRMs, in which 2 harbored quasispecies with more than one class of DRMs. Treatment modifications were recommended for these cases. The paper discusses the identification of drug resistance mutations in patients, suggesting that some had virological failure.",The paper's mention of sequencing failures due to low viral loads and the identification of drug resistance mutations in the context of treatment modification implies that some individuals had experienced virological failure.
37537871,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,The study does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial; it focuses on the diagnostic evaluation of the sequencing methods.,The paper does not indicate that the patients were enrolled in a clinical trial.
37537871,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Viral RNA in the pellet was extracted using QIAamp Viral RNA Kit, according to the manufacturer’s instructions. Then, 8 μL of extracted RNA was subjected to DNA removal using ezDNase™, reverse transcription with LunaScript RT SuperMix (5X), and amplification targeting the long genomic region (NC_001802.1: 1413–7363, amplicon length: 5951 base pairs) using the reagents and cycling conditions described in Supplemental Table 2. Amplicons were purified with 0.5×AMPure XP beads (for nanopore sequencing) or with QIAquick PCR Purification Kit (for Illumina) and quantified with Qubit® dsDNA HS Assay Kits This part describing RNA extraction, reverse transcription and amplification meaning that the viral load was tested, and the ARV drug resistance was tested these mean the individual has received ARV drugs, and amplify and sequencing detected the drug resistance mutations. So the paper describes that individuals has receive arav drugs.  Viral load (copies per μL) of each RNA sample was determined using GeneSig Standard Real-time PCR Detection Kit for HIV-1 and Oasig Lyophilized One Step qRT-PCR MasterMix Kit. Viral load was test in this paper; So the paper was detected drug resistance mutaitons. All the meaning from these sentences means the recpeients has received drugs environment.  In this case, the individuals have previously received ARV drugs.","The context of the study involves patients from whom samples were collected for drug resistance profiling, indicating that they had received ARV drugs before sequencin."
37537871,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, PI","While the specific drug classes received by individuals are not detailed in the paper, the study focuses on sequencing and identifying resistance mutations associated with NRTIs, NNRTIs, and PIs.","The paper focuses on sequencing and identifying resistance mutations associated with NRTIs, NNRTIs, and PIs, indicating that individuals had received drugs from these classes before sequencing."
37537871,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"ABT, DDI, FTC, 3TC, DOR, ETN, NVP, RPV","The paper mentions the detection of resistance mutations associated with specific drugs such as abacavir (ABC), didanosine (DDI), emtricitabine (FTC), lamivudine (3TC), doravirine (DOR), etravirine (ETN), nevirapine (NVP), and rilpivirine (RPV).","The paper mentions the detection of resistance mutations associated with specific drugs, suggesting that individuals had received these drugs before sequencing."
