37674678,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"In our study, 1,393 ART-naïve individuals newly diagnosed with HIV-1 were enrolled between January 1, 2019 and November 31, 2021. We sequenced and analyzed 1,161 samples obtained from 1,393 HIV-1 infected individuals in our research.","The paper clearly states that the study involved ART-naïve individuals newly diagnosed with HIV-1, and sequences were obtained from these individuals. This indicates that the paper does report HIV sequences from patient samples."
37674678,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"The degree of drug resistance to each ART drug was divided into five levels: susceptible (S, 0-9), potential low resistance (PLR, 10-14), low-level resistance (LR, 15-29), intermediate-level resistance (IR, 30-59), and high-level resistance categories (HR, ≥60). TDR was detected among ART-naïve individuals, and sequences classified as low-, intermediate-, or high-level resistance were designated as drug resistance according to the WHO drug resistance report (6).","The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing. It focuses on genotypic resistance analysis using sequences obtained from patient samples, but there is no indication of in vitro testing of drug susceptibility."
