37878637,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"A cohort study was conducted from 2018--2020 among 311 adolescents living with perinatally acquired HIV (APHI) receiving antiretroviral therapy (ART) in one of the selected health facilities within the ""Resistance Evolution among Adolescents in Yaoundé and its surroundings"" (READY-study) in the Centre region of Cameroon. Sequencing of protease and reverse transcriptase regions was performed for participants experiencing virological failure, VF, (Plasma viral load, PVL ≥ 1000 RNA copies/ml).","The paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples as it mentions sequencing of protease and reverse transcriptase regions for participants experiencing virological failure, and it describes the collection and analysis of HIV-1 RNA from plasma samples of adolescents living with perinatally acquired HIV who were receiving antiretroviral therapy in Cameroon."
37878637,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"A cohort study was conducted from 2018--2020 among 311 adolescents living with perinatally acquired HIV (APHI) receiving antiretroviral therapy (ART) in one of the selected health facilities within the ""Resistance Evolution among Adolescents in Yaoundé and its surroundings"" (READY-study) in the Centre region of Cameroon. Participants were recruited following consecutive, and exhaustive sampling. Follow-up was performed at enrollment (T1), at 6 months (T2), and at 12 months (T3). Included in the current analysis were only participants failing first- and second-line ART with plasma viral load (PVL) ≥ 1000 RNA copies/ml ( Table 1 ).","The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data. It focuses on sequencing and genotypic resistance testing using plasma samples from patients experiencing virological failure, but does not discuss any laboratory experiments related to drug susceptibility."
37878637,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,The data underlying the results presented in the study are available from figshare (https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.22779836).,"The paper mentions that the data underlying the results are available from figshare, which indicates that the sequences have been made publicly available."
37878637,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,,,"The paper does not provide the specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates. It mentions that the sequences were obtained and edited using software, but does not list the accession numbers. Data were analyzed using SPSS version 22, with p < 0.05 considered statistically significant. A comparison of means and medians of various characteristics was done using the paired t-test. Chi-square and Fisher's exact tests were used for determining associations between qualitative variables. Study endpoints were defined as CD4 count < 250 cells/mm3 and PVL > 5 log RNA/mL. Cox proportional hazard regression models were used to estimate hazard ratios (HRs) of disease progression to each endpoint stratified by HIV-1 subtype, adjusting for the presence of drug resistance mutations, gender, ART line, adherence, and duration on ART. Kaplan Meier curves were used to examine time to CD4 count decline to < 250 cells/mm3 and VL > 5 log10 RNA copies/mL on ART across subtypes, with the use of the log-rank test to test the significance of observed differences between groups. Survival curves were drawn using SPSS version 22. Moreover, median CD4 cell rise and PVL decline over time were determined and presented as figures. The data for this analysis were not included in the extracted information from the paper."
37878637,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,141,"Of the 141 participants in VF enrolled, the male-female ratio was 1:1; mean age was 15 (±3) years; and median [IQR] duration on ART was 51 [46--60] months. Of these, 141 participants with PVL ≥ 1000 RNA copies/mL, and whose samples were successfully sequenced were included in the current assessment.",The paper mentions that 141 participants experiencing virological failure had successful sequences obtained and were included in the analysis.
37878637,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Cameroon,"A cohort study was conducted from 2018--2020 among 311 adolescents living with perinatally acquired HIV (APHI) receiving antiretroviral therapy (ART) in one of the selected health facilities within the ""Resistance Evolution among Adolescents in Yaoundé and its surroundings"" (READY-study) in the Centre region of Cameroon.",The study was conducted among adolescents living with perinatally acquired HIV in urban and rural settings of the Center region of Cameroon.
37878637,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2018-2020,"A cohort study was conducted from 2018--2020 among 311 adolescents living with perinatally acquired HIV (APHI) receiving antiretroviral therapy (ART) in one of the selected health facilities within the Resistance Evolution among Adolescents in Yaoundé and its surroundings""  (READY-study) in the Centre region of Cameroon.",The paper states that the cohort study was conducted from 2018 to 2020.
37878637,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"HIV-1 RNA extraction was performed from 1000 μL of plasma aliquots and an initial 2-hour refrigerated centrifugation step at 14 000 rpm to concentrate viral RNA was also performed. HIV-1 RNA was extracted manually from 140 μL of plasma using the QIAGEN protocol (QIAamp® DNA Minikit; QIAGEN, Courtaboeuf, France). GRT was done when the viral load was > 1000 copies/mL using an in-house protocol. Eight in-house primers (B, F, SEQ1, SEQ2, SEQ3, SEQ4, SEQ5, TAK3) that completely covered the protease and reverse-transcriptase regions in the pol gene fragment (~1600 base pairs) were used for sequencing. PBCR products were sequenced using the Applied Biosystems 3500 genetic analyzer; the sequences thus obtained were edited using the Recall CDC  Atlanta GA USA software and drug resistance mutations (DRMs) interpreted using Stanford HIVdb.v8.8; Subtyping was done using a rapid subtyping tool, Stanford HIVdb v8.9, and confirmed by MEGA X for molecular phylogeny using the Neighbor-Joining algorithm14, maximum likelihood method14 and a 500 replicates bootstrap value>80% for subtype assignation. Assessment of potential emerging variants was performed using Splits Tree 4 v4.6 software[15] and genetic breakpoints were identified using the Recombinant Detection program version 4  (RDP4)16. Reference sequences included in the phylogenetic analysis were downloaded following a blast search from the National Center for Biotechnology Information website; https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/.","The paper described the extraction of HIV-1 RNA from plasma samples and direct sequencing of the PCR products, which implies that cloning was not performed prior to sequencing."
37878637,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Protease and Reverse Transcriptase,"Sequencing of protease and reverse transcriptase regions was performed for participants experiencing virological failure, VF, (Plasma viral load, PVL ≥ 1000 RNA copies/ml). Moreover, plasma aliquots (for PVL and HIV genotypic resistance testing, GRT) were obtained after centrifugation at 1600 rpm for 10 minutes and stored at −80°C for further analyses. Genotypic resistance testing (GRT) was performed for these participants failing treatment. Eight in-house primers (B, F, SEQ1, SEQ2, SEQ3, SEQ4, SEQ5, TAK3) that completely covered the protease and reverse-transcriptase regions in the pol gene fragment (~1600 base pairs) were used for sequencing.",The paper specifies that sequencing was performed on the protease and reverse transcriptase regions of the pol gene fragment.
37878637,10,What method was used for sequencing?,PCR products were sequenced using the Applied Biosystems 3500 genetic analyzer.,PCR products were sequenced using the Applied Biosystems 3500 genetic analyzer; the sequences thus obtained were edited using the Recall CDC Atlanta GA USA software and drug resistance mutations (DRMs) interpreted using Stanford HIVdb.v8.8.,The paper mentions that PCR products were sequenced using the Applied Biosystems 3500 genetic analyzer.
37878637,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma and whole blood samples were sequenced,"Following enrolment, ten mL of whole blood were collected from each participant and transported on icepacks within 6 hours to the virology laboratory of the Chantal Biya international reference center (CIRCB), Yaoundé, Cameroon. HIV-1 RNA extraction was performed from 1000 μL of plasma aliquots and an initial 2-hour refrigerated centrifugation step at 14 000 rpm to concentrate viral RNA was also performed. HIV-1 RNA was extracted manually from 140 μL of plasma using the QIAGEN protocol (QIAamp® DNA Minikit; QIAGEN, Courtaboeuf, France).","The paper mentions that plasma aliquots were obtained for HIV genotypic resistance testing, and 140 μL of plasma was used for sequencing."
37878637,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"A cohort study was conducted from 2018--2020 among 311 adolescents living with perinatally acquired HIV (APHI) receiving antiretroviral therapy (ART) in one of the selected health facilities within the ""Resistance Evolution among Adolescents in Yaoundé and its surroundings"" (READY-study) in the Centre region of Cameroon. Sequencing of protease and reverse transcriptase regions was performed for participants experiencing virological failure, VF, (Plasma viral load, PVL ≥ 1000 RNA copies/ml). Genotypic resistance testing (GRT) was performed for these participants failing treatment.","The paper clearly states that sequencing was performed for participants experiencing virological failure, indicating that sequences were obtained from such individuals."
37878637,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"A cohort study was conducted from 2018--2020 among 311 adolescents living with perinatally acquired HIV (APHI) receiving antiretroviral therapy (ART) in one of the selected health facilities within the Resistance Evolution among Adolescents in Yaoundé and its surroundings""  (READY-study) in the Centre region of Cameroon. Participants were recruited following consecutive, and exhaustive sampling. Follow-up was performed at enrollment (T1), at 6 months (T2), and at 12 months (T3). Included in the current analysis were only participants failing first- and second-line ART with plasma viral load (PVL) ≥ 1000 RNA copies/ml ( Table 1 ).",The paper describes a cohort study and does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial.
37878637,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Included in the study were APHI; aged 10--19 years, receiving a standard reverse transcriptase inhibitor-based first- or ritonavir-boosted protease inhibitor-based second-line ART regimen for at least 6 months, provided written assent, and informed consent from their legal guardian(s), and irrespective of exposure to the prevention of mother to child transmission (PMTCT) antiretrovirals. HIV-1 RNA extraction was performed from 1000 μL of plasma aliquots and an initial 2-hour refrigerated centrifugation step at 14 000 rpm to concentrate viral RNA was also performed. HIV-1 RNA was extracted manually from 140 μL of plasma using the QIAGEN protocol (QIAamp® DNA Minikit; QIAGEN, Courtaboeuf, France). GRT was done when the viral load was > 1000 copies/mL using an in-house protocol.","The paper includes adolescents aged 10 to 19 years, receiving a standard reverse transcriptase inhibitor-based first- or ritonavir-boosted protease inhibitor-based second-line ART regimen for at least 6 months, which indicates that sequences were obtained for individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
37878637,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, PI, NNRTI","Included in the study were APHI; aged 10--19 years, receiving a standard reverse transcriptase inhibitor-based first- or ritonavir-boosted protease inhibitor-based second-line ART regimen for at least 6 months, provided written assent, and informed consent from their legal guardian(s), and irrespective of exposure to the prevention of mother to child transmission (PMTCT) antiretrovirals. HIV-1 RNA extraction was performed from 1000 μL of plasma aliquots and an initial 2-hour refrigerated centrifugation step at 14 000 rpm to concentrate viral RNA was also performed. HIV-1 RNA was extracted manually from 140 μL of plasma using the QIAGEN protocol (QIAamp® DNA Minikit; QIAGEN, Courtaboeuf, France). GRT was done when the viral load was > 1000 copies/mL using an in-house protocol.","The paper mentioned that participants were receiving a standard reverse transcriptase inhibitor-based first- or ritonavir-boosted protease inhibitor-based second-line ART regimen, which includes NRTIs, PIs, and NNRTIs."
37878637,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"TDF, 3TC, EFV, DTG","Most of the participants (34.5%, 31.3%, and 31.7%) were on a TDF + 3TC + EFV-based regimen (Table 2). Eighty-two (58.2%) participants were receiving TDF + 3TC + EFV (d4T+3TC+EFV) and seventy-two (51.1%) were receiving tenofovir disoproxil = TDF + lamivudine = 3TC + dolutegravir =  DTG as a febrile regimen. The drugs utilized are the following: Tenofovir (TDF), Lamivudine (3TC) Efavirenz, DJT","The paper mentions that most participants were on a TDF + 3TC + EFV-based regimen, and some were receiving DTG, which specifies the drugs received before sample sequencing."
37880705,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations (PDRM) along with the analysis of HIV-1 variant dynamics. We identified nine studies and analyzed 1070 retrieved HIV-1 pol sequences in this systematic review.,The paper mentions that HIV-1 pol sequences were retrieved from studies conducted among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals and analyzed for the presence of pretreatment drug resistance mutations. This indicates that the paper does report HIV sequences from patient samples.
37880705,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"This systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia. The Calibrated Population Resistance (CPR) tool Version 8.1 and the REGA HIV-1 Subtyping Tool Version 3 were used to determine the PDRM and HIV-1 genetic diversity, respectively.",The paper focuses on the occurrence of pretreatment drug resistance mutations and does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data.
37880705,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,"Sequences of the included studies were downloaded from GenBank if they were publicly available and, if they were not found online, study authors were contacted for the respective sequences.","The paper indicates that sequences were downloaded from GenBank if they were publicly available, suggesting that the sequences were made publicly available."
37880705,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not applicable,No evidence,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
37880705,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,1070,We identified nine studies and analyzed 1070 retrieved HIV-1 pol sequences in this systematic review.,The paper states that 1070 retrieved HIV-1 pol sequences were analyzed in the systematic review.
37880705,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Ethiopia,"Ethiopia is among the highly HIV-affected countries, with reported 12,000 and 12,000 AIDS-related deaths and incidents as per reports from 2021. The current study confirmed the HIV-1 subtype C virus as the predominant clade in Ethiopia, similar to other eastern and southern African countries like South Africa",The paper focuses on HIV-1 variant dynamics and pretreatment drug resistance among ART-naïve individuals in Ethiopia.
37880705,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2003 to 2018,HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations (PDRM) along with the analysis of HIV-1 variant dynamics.,The paper mentions that the studies from which the sequences were retrieved were conducted between 2003 and 2018.
37880705,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"Sequences of the included studies were downloaded from GenBank if they were publicly available and, if they were not found online, study authors were contacted for the respective sequences.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
37880705,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Pol gene (Protease and partial RT),"Accordingly, we included 1070 sequences (from the total of 1226 retrieved sequences) that have full protease and partial RT.",The paper specifies that the analysis included sequences that have full protease and partial RT.
37880705,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Not applicable,No evidence,The paper does not specify the method used for sequencing the HIV samples.
37880705,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Not applicable,No evidence,The paper does not provide information on the type of samples that were sequenced.
37880705,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,The HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations.,"The paper specifically mentions that the individuals were ART-naïve, indicating that they had not experienced virological failure on a treatment regimen."
37880705,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"Thus, this systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia.",The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial. It is a systematic review.
37880705,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,The HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations.,"The paper specifies that the individuals were ART-naïve, indicating that they had not previously received ARV drugs."
37880705,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not applicable,The HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations.,The paper does not mention any drug classes received by individuals before sample sequencing as they were ART-naïve.
