37896785,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"The study material was blood plasma samples from HIV-infected pregnant women: 31 women showed virological failure of ART, and 30 women had not previously received therapy.","The paper discusses the collection and analysis of HIV-1 sequences from blood plasma samples of pregnant women, indicating that HIV sequences were reported from patient samples."
37896785,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,The aim of our work was to analyze subtypic structure and drug-resistant variants of HIV in pregnant women in Ho Chi Minh City.,The paper discusses drug resistance mutations but does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility assays or data.
37896785,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,The nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained and deposited in GenBank (numbers OQ215322-OQ215382).,"The paper explicitly states that the nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were deposited in GenBank, indicating that they were made publicly available."
37896785,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,OQ215322-OQ215382,The nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained and deposited in GenBank (numbers OQ215322-OQ215382).,"The paper provides the specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, which are listed in the results section."
37896785,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,61,The study material was blood plasma samples collected in 2021 from 61 pregnant women in need of PMTCT in Ho Chi Minh City with a viral load above 500 copies per ml of blood plasma.,"The paper mentions that blood plasma samples were collected from 61 pregnant women for the study, indicating the number of individuals from whom samples were obtained."
37896785,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Vietnam,"The study material was blood plasma samples from HIV-infected pregnant women in Ho Chi Minh City, South Vietnam. The study material was blood plasma samples collected in 2021 from 61 pregnant women in need of PMTCT in Ho Chi Minh City with a viral load above 500 copies per ml of blood plasma.","The paper specifies that the samples were collected from pregnant women in Ho Chi Minh City, South Vietnam."
37896785,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2021,"The study material was blood plasma samples collected in 2021 from 61 pregnant women in need of PMTCT in Ho Chi Minh City with a viral load above 500 copies per ml of blood plasma. In the survey group, 31 women showed virological failure of ART, and 30 women had not previously received therapy. All samples were transferred anonymously. Molecular genetic studies were carried out at the Pasteur Institute in St. Petersburg. Quantitative analysis of HIV RNA was carried out with a commercial kit, AmpliSens® HIV-Monitor-FRT (Central Research Institute of Epidemiology, Moscow, Russia) with a sensitivity threshold of 500 copies/mL. For samples with a detectable viral load, reverse transcription and PCR were performed, followed by Sanger sequencing using the AmpliSens HIVResist-Seq (Central Research Institute of Epidemiology, Moscow, Russia) commercial kit. HIV-1 genotyping was performed based on analysis of the nucleotide sequences of the 1285 nt pol gene region encoding the protease (PR) and part of the reverse transcriptase (RT) in the 2085--3369 nt region.",The paper mentions that the blood plasma samples were collected in 2021.
37896785,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"For samples with a detectable viral load, reverse transcription and PCR were performed, followed by Sanger sequencing using the AmpliSens HIVResist-Seq (Central Research Institute of Epidemiology, Moscow, Russia) commercial kit. HIV-1 genotyping was performed based on analysis of the nucleotide sequences of the 1285 nt pol gene region encoding the protease (PR) and part of the reverse transcriptase (RT) in the 2085--3369 nt region. The coordinates given are for HIV HXB2 in the GenBank database (K03455.1). Sequencing reaction products were analyzed using an ABI Prism 3500 genetic analyzer (Applied Biosystems, Waltham, MA, USA).",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It describes direct sequencing of PCR products.
37896785,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,pol,HIV-1 genotyping and mutation detection were performed based on analysis of the nucleotide sequences of the *pol* gene region. HIV-1 genotyping was performed based on analysis of the nucleotide sequences of the 1285 nt *pol* gene region encoding the protease (PR) and part of the reverse transcriptase (RT) in the 2085--3369 nt region.,The paper specifies that the nucleotide sequences of the *pol* gene region were analyzed for genotyping and mutation detection.
