37976185,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Not reported,"Methods. We used New York City surveillance and partner services data to measure the effect of PrEP use (tenofovir disoproxil fumarate/tenofivir alafenamide fumarate with emtricitabine) history on the baseline prevalence of M184I/V mutations in people with HIV diagnosed in 2015--2022. PrEP use was categorized as ""recent"" (defined as PrEP stopped ≤90 days before diagnosis), ""past"" (PrEP stopped >90 days before diagnosis), or ""no known use."" Resistance-associated mutations were determined using the Stanford algorithm.","The paper does not specific which specific genes were sequenced, it focuses on the M184I/V mutations which is a polymorphism in the reverse transcriptase gene."
37976185,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Not reported,"Methods. We used New York City surveillance and partner services data to measure the effect of PrEP use (tenofovir disiproxil fumarate/tenofivir alafenamide fumarate with emtricitabine) history on the baseline prevalence of M184I/V mutations in people with HIV diagnosed in 2015--2022. We included people with HIV newly diagnosed between 2015 and 2022, assigned for partner services, for whom a genotype obtained within 30 days of diagnosis was available in the NYC HIV Surveillance Registry (henceforth, Registry).","The paper does not mention the sequencing method used, it focuses on the prevalence of mutations."
37976185,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"Methods. We used New York City surveillance and partner services data to measure the effect of PrEP use (tenofovir disoproxil fumarate/tenofivir alafenamide fumarate with emtricitabine) history on the baseline prevalence of M184I/V mutations in people with HIV diagnosed in 2015--2022. We included people with HIV newly diagnosed between 2015 and 2022, assigned for partner services, for whom a genotype obtained within 30 days of diagnosis was available in the NYC HIV Surveillance Registry (henceforth, Registry). HIV-related laboratory results (CD4 cell count, HIV viral load [VL], and HIV-1 genotype sequences [Sanger or consensus sequences when next-generation sequencing is conducted]) are reported to the health department and stored in the Registry and laboratory databases.",The paper mentioned collecting HIV-related laboratory results including HIV-1 genotype sequences which are typically obtained from plasma samples.
37976185,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Not reported,"Methods. We used New York City surveillance and partner services data to measure the effect of PrEP use (tenofovir disoproxil fumarate/tenofivir alafenamide fumarate with emtricitabine) history on the baseline prevalence of M184I/V mutations in people with HIV diagnosed in 2015--2022. We included people with HIV newly diagnosed between 2015 and 2022, assigned for partner services, for whom a genotype obtained within 30 days of diagnosis was available in the NYC HIV Surveillance Registry (henceforth, Registry).",The paper mentioned including people with new diagnosed HIV in 2015 to 2022 which means they are all treatment naïve.
37976185,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"We included people with HIV newly diagnosed between 2015 and 2022, assigned for partner services, for whom a genotype obtained within 30 days of diagnosis was available in the NYC HIV Surveillance Registry (henceforth, Registry). We used New York City surveillance and partner services data to measure the effect of PrEP use (tenofovir disoproxil fumarate/tenofivir alafenamide fumarate with emtricitabine) history on the baseline prevalence of M184I/V mutations in people with HIV diagnosed in 2015--2022. We described PrEP use history, AHI, and the prevalence of M184I/V and K65R mutations in a retrospective cohort of people with newly diagnosed HIV in 2015--2022. We measured the association of PrEP use history and timing with the presence of M184I/V at their baseline genotype obtained within 30 days of diagnosis, in people with or without AHI respectively.","The paper discusses a retrospective cohort study using surveillance and partner services data, not a clinical trial."
