38142692,10,What method was used for sequencing?,,,"The paper does not mention any sequencing methods, as it does not involve sequencing."
38142692,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,None,"In this retrospective observational cohort study, we used routinely collected, de-identified data from 59 primary health-care facilities in eThekwini Municipality, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa. We included people living with HIV aged 15 years or older with virological failure (defined as two consecutive viral loads of ≥1000 copies per mL at least 56 days apart) on first-line NNRTI-based ART containing tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) and who switched to second-line ART. Our primary outcomes were retention in care and viral suppression (<50 copies per mL) at 12 months after starting second-line treatment. We used modified Poisson regression models to compare these outcomes between second-line regimens (zidovudine [AZT]/emtricitabine or lamivudine [XTC]/DTG; TDF/XTC/DTG; and AZT/XTC/LPV/r).","The paper does not mention any type of clinical or laboratory specimens that were sequenced, as it does not involve sequencing."
38142692,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"In this retrospective observational cohort study, we used routinely collected, de-identified data from 59 primary health-care facilities in eThekwini Municipality, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa. We included people living with HIV aged 15 years or older with virological failure (defined as two consecutive viral loads of ≥1000 copies per mL at least 56 days apart) on first-line NNRTI-based ART containing tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) and who switched to second-line ART. Our primary outcomes were retention in care and viral suppression (<50 copies per mL) at 12 months after starting second-line treatment. We used modified Poisson regression models to compare these outcomes between second-line regimens (zidovudine [AZT]/emtricitabine or lamivudine [XTC]/DTG; TDF/XTC/DTG; and AZT/XTC/LPV/r).",The paper does not report any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen. It focuses on clinical outcomes rather than sequencing data.
38142692,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"We did a retrospective observational cohort study with de-identified, routinely collected data from South Africa's ART programme in 59 of approximately 100 public sector primary health-care clinics in the eThekwini Municipality of the KwaZulu-Natal province.",The paper describes a retrospective observational cohort study and does not mention that the patients were in a clinical trial.
38142692,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"In this retrospective observational cohort study, we used routinely collected, de-identified data from 59 primary health-care facilities in eThekwini Municipality, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa. We included people living with HIV aged 15 years or older with virological failure (defined as two consecutive viral loads of ≥1000 copies per mL at least 56 days apart) on first-line NNRTI-based ART containing tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) and who switched to second-line ART. Our primary outcomes were retention in care and viral suppression (<50 copies per mL) at 12 months after starting second-line treatment. We used modified Poisson regression models to compare these outcomes between second-line regimens (zidovudine [AZT]/emtricitabine or lamivudine [XTC]/DTG; TDF/XTC/DTG; and AZT/XTC/LPV/r).",The paper does not report any sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs. It focuses on treatment outcomes rather than sequencing data.
38142692,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,,,"The paper does not report any sequences or drug classes received by individuals before sequencing, as it does not involve sequencing."
38142692,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,,,"The paper does not report any sequences or drugs received by individuals before sequencing, as it does not involve sequencing."
38152686,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"To describe the clinical case of an HIV/Tuberculosis coinfected patient who developed Human Immunodeficieny Virus (HIV) treatment failure during dolutegravir therapy.; The viral load was 437,927 cp/mL (Log = 5.64). After 8 months, therapeutic failure was verified. Genotyping was requested, with detection of the *H51Y* and *E157Q* mutations in the integrase.","The paper describes a clinical case of an HIV/Tuberculosis coinfected patient, indicating the presence of HIV sequences from patient samples. Specifically, it mentions the detection of mutations in the integrase gene of HIV, which implies that HIV sequences were obtained from the patient for genotyping purposes."
38152686,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"To describe the clinical case of an HIV/Tuberculosis coinfected patient who developed Human Immunodeficieny Virus (HIV) treatment failure during dolutegravir therapy.; The viral load was 437,927 cp/mL (Log = 5.64). After 8 months, therapeutic failure was verified. Genotyping was requested, with detection of the *H51Y* and *E157Q* mutations in the integrase.",The paper focuses on a clinical case report of an HIV/Tuberculosis coinfected patient and discusses genotypic resistance mutations but does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing or data.
38152686,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,Information regarding this case is available upon request.,The paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available; it states that information regarding the case is available upon request.
38152686,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not reported,No evidence,"The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, focusing instead on the clinical case and the genotypic mutations observed."
38152686,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,1,"To describe the clinical case of an HIV/Tuberculosis coinfected patient who developed Human Immunodeficieny Virus (HIV) treatment failure during dolutegravir therapy.; A 29-year-old male patient was admitted with a right cervical mass associated with fever, dry cough, hyporexia, and myalgia for more than 2 weeks, as well as neurological symptoms of headache and sudden hemiparesis.","The paper describes a single 29-year-old male patient who had samples obtained for HIV sequencing, focusing on his clinical case and the genotypic mutations observed."
38152686,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Brazil,"In Brazil, TB-HIV coinfection is extremely prevalent. Rifampicin, which consists of a rifamycin with fundamental bactericidal action for the treatment of TB, interacts with DTG by inducing the liver enzymes UGT1A1 and CYP3A, thus reducing the plasma concentrations of this drug.","The paper mentions that TB-HIV coinfection is extremely prevalent in Brazil, indicating that the sequenced samples were obtained from Brazil."
38152686,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,Not reported,No evidence,"The paper does not provide specific years during which the sequenced samples were obtained, focusing instead on the clinical case and the events surrounding it."
38152686,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"To describe the clinical case of an HIV/Tuberculosis coinfected patient who developed Human Immunodeficieny Virus (HIV) treatment failure during dolutegravir therapy.; genotyping was requested, which revealed *H51Y* and *E157Q* mutations, which are associated with resistance to INIs, including DTG, and *K70E* and *M184V* mutations in the reverse transcriptase genes.","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing, focusing instead on the genotypic mutations observed directly from the clinical case."
38152686,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,integrase and reverse transcriptase,"Genotyping was requested, which revealed *H51Y* and *E157Q* mutations, which are associated with resistance to INIs, including DTG, and *K70E* and *M184V* mutations in the reverse transcriptase genes.","The paper mentions the detection of mutations in the integrase gene and the reverse transcriptase genes, indicating that these genes were sequenced."
38152686,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Not reported,No evidence,"The paper does not specify the method used for sequencing, focusing instead on the clinical case and the genotypic mutations observed."
38152686,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Not reported,No evidence,"The paper does not specify the type of samples that were sequenced, focusing instead on the clinical case and the genotypic mutations observed."
38152686,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"art was switched to TDF/3TC/EFZ, and genotyping was requested, which revealed H51Y and E157Q mutations, which are associated with resistance to INIs, including DTG, and K70E and M184V mutations in the reverse transcriptase genes. The patient was then treated with a rescue regimen of TDF/3TC/DRV600 mg/RTV100 mg, reaching a VL less than 40 cp/mL, 6 months later.","The paper describes the clinical case of a patient who experienced therapeutic failure and developed resistance mutations, indicating that sequences were obtained from an individual with virological failure."
38152686,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"To describe the clinical case of an HIV/Tuberculosis coinfected patient who developed Human Immunodeficieny Virus (HIV) treatment failure during dolutegravir therapy.; A 29-year-old male patient was admitted with a right cervical mass associated with fever, dry cough, hyporexia, and myalgia for more than 2 weeks, as well as neurological symptoms of headache and sudden hemiparesis.","The paper describes a case report of a single patient, not a clinical trial, focusing on his clinical course and the genotypic mutations observed."
38152686,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Antiretroviral therapy was initiated with Tenofovir/Lamivudine and Dolutegravir (TDF/3TC and DTG), the latter at a dose of 50 mg/day, as was a regimen for tuberculosis. After 8 months, therapeutic failure was verified. Genotyping was requested, with detection of the H51Y and E157Q mutations in the integrase. ART was switched to TDF/3TC/EFZ, and genotyping was requested, which revealed H51Y and E157Q mutations, which are associated with resistance to INIs, including DTG, and K70E and M184V mutations in the reverse transcriptase genes.","The paper describes a patient who had received antiretroviral therapy with Tenofovir/Lamivudine and Dolutegravir, and later switched to TDF/3TC/EFZ, and genotyping was requested, which revealed mutatiosn associated with resistance to INIs, indicating that sequences were obtained after the patient received ARV drugs."
38152686,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, INSTI, NNRTI","Antiretroviral therapy was initiated with Tenofovir/Lamivudine and Dolutegravir (TDF/3TC and DTG), the latter at a dose of 50 mg/day, as was a regimen for tuberculosis. After 8 months, therapeutic failure was verified. Genotyping was requested, with detection of the H51Y and E157Q mutations in the integrase. ART was switched to TDF/3TC/EFZ, and genotyping was requested, which revealed H51Y and E157Q mutations, which are associated with resistance to INIs, including DTG, and K70E and M184V mutations in the reverse transcriptase genes.","The paper describes the patient received ART initiated with Tenofovir/Lamivudine (TDF/3TC, which are NRTIs) and Dolutegravir (an INSTI), and after 8 months switched to TDF/3TC/EFZ (at a later point switched to Efavirenz, which is an NNRTI), and genotyping was requested, which revealed mutations associated with resistance to INSTIs and K70E and M184V, which are mutations associated with resistance to NRTIs in the reverse transcriptase gene, indicating that drug classes received before sequencing were  NRTI, INSTI, NNRTI."
38152686,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Tenofovir, lamivudine, dolutegravir, efavirenz","Antiretroviral therapy was initiated with Tenofovir/Lamivudine and Dolutegravir (TDF/3TC and DTG), the latter at a dose of 50 mg/day, as was a regimen for tuberculosis. After 8 months, therapeutic failure was verified. Genotyping was requested, with detection of the H51Y and E157Q mutations in the integrase. ART was switched to TDF/3TC/EFZ, and genotyping was requested, which revealed H51Y and E157Q mutations, which are associated with resistance to INIs, including DTG, and K70E and M184V mutations in the reverse transcriptase genes.","The paper describes the patient received ART initiated with Tenofovir/Lamivudine (TDF/3TC) and Dolutegravir (DTG), and after 8 months switched to TDF/3TC/EFZ (at a later point switched to Efavirenz), and genotyping was requested, which revealed mutations associated with resistance to INSTIs and K70E and M184V, which are mutations associated with resistance to NRTIs in the reverse transcriptase gene, indicating that drugs received before sequencing DFG were Tenofovir, Lamivudine, Dolutegravir and Efavirenz."
38314093,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"This study undertakes a retrospective analysis of the epidemiological and clinical features of 195 HIV-positive cases in Meizhou, China, from May 1, 2018 to December 31, 2019. Among 195 HIV-infected individuals, 37 untreated patients were included for genotypic resistance testing, and Pro-RT gene sequences from the samples were obtained and analyzed for drug resistance-related mutations.","The paper discusses the study of HIV-positive individuals and mentions that serum samples were analyzed for drug resistance genotypes. It specifically states that Pro-RT gene sequences from the samples were obtained, indicating that HIV sequences from patient samples were reported."
38314093,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"An analysis of drug resistance genotypes indicated that, despite viral mutations conferring resistance to certain reverse transcriptase inhibitors, the first-line treatment regimen remained effective for patients in Meizhou. Notably, mutations resistant to protease inhibitors were infrequent (2.7%), suggesting that incorporating protease inhibitors into the treatment regimen may enhance therapeutic outcomes for local patients.",The paper focuses on genotypic resistance testing and the presence of drug resistance mutations in patient samples but does not mention any in vitro testing of drug susceptibility.
38314093,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,"Pro-RT gene sequences from the samples were obtained and analyzed for drug resistance-related mutations. Sequences were submitted to the Stanford University HIV resistance database (http://hivdb.stanford.EDU) for subtype identification, resistance loci, and drug sensitivity analysis.","The paper mentions that sequences were submitted to the Stanford University HIV resistance database for analysis, indicating that the sequences were made publicly available."
38314093,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not reported,,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates as it focuses on the analysis and results without detailing the accession numbers associated with the sequences.
38314093,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,37,"To elucidate the HIV-1 genotype drug resistance characteristics in HIV-infected people of Meizhou, serum samples from 37 untreated patients obtained from Meizhou People's Hospital were included.","The paper states that serum samples from 37 untreated patients were included for genotypic resistance testing, indicating that samples were obtained from 37 individuals."
38314093,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,China,"This study undertakes a retrospective analysis of the epidemiological and clinical features of 195 HIV-positive cases in Meizhou, China, from May 1, 2018 to December 31, 2019.","The paper specifies that the study was conducted in Meizhou, China, and the samples were obtained from Meizhou People's Hospital."
38314093,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,"Samples were collected from 2008 to 2019, and the sequenced samples were from 2018 to 2019","In this study, serum samples collected from the HIV Confirmatory Laboratory of Meizhou People's Hospital Medical Laboratory Center (From May 2008 to December 2019) were analyzed. This study undertakes a retrospective analysis of the epidemiological and clinical features of 195 HIV-positive cases in Meizhou, China, from May 1, 2018 to December 31, 2019.","The paper mentions that serum samples were collected from May 2008 to December 2019 for analysis, and the retrospective study was between 2018 to 2019."
38314093,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,Not reported,"An analysis of drug resistance genotypes indicated that, despite viral mutations conferring resistance to certain reverse transcriptase inhibitors, the first-line treatment regimen remained effective for patients in Meizhou. Notably, mutations resistant to protease inhibitors were infrequent (2.7%), suggesting that incorporating protease inhibitors into the treatment regimen may enhance therapeutic outcomes for local patients.",There's no evidence indicating that the samples were cloned prior to sequencing.
38314093,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Protease and reverse transcriptase genes,"Pro-RT gene sequences from the samples were obtained and analyzed for drug resistance-related mutations. In brief, cDNA containing the protease-reverse transcriptase (PR-RT) sequence of HIV-1 was amplified and subjected to high-throughput sequencing.","The paper mentions that Pro-RT gene sequences from the samples were obtained and analyzed, indicating that both protease and reverse transcriptase genes were sequenced."
38314093,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Not reported,"In brief, cDNA containing the protease-reverse transcriptase (PR-RT) sequence of HIV-1 was amplified and subjected to high-throughput sequencing.","The paper mentions that cDNA containing the PR-RT sequence was subjected to high-throughput sequencing. However, it does not provide specific details on the sequencing method used."
38314093,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Serum,HIV-infected blood samples were sent to the Guangdong AIDS Prevention Center for genotypic resistance testing.,"The paper mentions that serum samples from 37 untreated patients were included for genotypic resistance testing, indicating that serum was the type of sample sequenced."
38314093,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"To elucidate the HIV-1 genotype drug resistance characteristics in HIV-infected people of Meizhou, serum samples from 37 untreated patients obtained from Meizhou People's Hospital were included.","The paper mentioned that samples were obtained from 37 untreated patients, and they were infected through various routes: heterosexual transmission (75.68%, 28/37), homosexual transmission (8.11%, 3/37), mother-to-child transmission (2.70%, 1/37), and unclear transmission (13.51%, 5/37), and the study mainly focus on the study of  virsus transmission route."
38314093,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"This study undertakes a retrospective analysis of the epidemiological and clinical features of 195 HIV-positive cases in Meizhou, China, from May 1, 2018 to December 31, 2019.",The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial. It describes a retrospective analysis of epidemiological and clinical features of HIV-positive cases.
38314093,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"To elucidate the HIV-1 genotype drug resistance characteristics in HIV-infected people of Meizhou, serum samples from 37 untreated patients obtained from Meizhou People’s Hospital were included.","The paper focused on untreated patients who were included in the study, hence it did not report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
38314093,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not reported,"To elucidate the HIV-1 genotype drug resistance characteristics in HIV-infected people of Meizhou, serum samples from 37 untreated patients obtained from Meizhou People’s Hospital were included.","The paper focused on untreated patients who were included in the study, hence it did not report the drug classes which were received by individuals before sample sequencing."
38314093,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not reported,"To elucidate the HIV-1 genotype drug resistance characteristics in HIV-infected people of Meizhou, serum samples from 37 untreated patients obtained from Meizhou People’s Hospital were included.","The paper focused on untreated patients who were included in the study, hence it did not report the drugs which were received by individuals before sample sequencing."
38427738,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"To elucidate INSTI resistance mechanisms, we propagated HIV-1 in the presence of escalating concentrations of the INSTI dolutegravir. HIV-1 became resistant to dolutegravir by sequentially acquiring mutations in the envelope glycoprotein and the nucleocapsid protein.","The paper does not discuss obtaining HIV sequences from patient samples. Instead, it focuses on laboratory-adapted strains of HIV-1 and the mutations acquired during propagation in cell lines. The study aims to understand the resistance mechanisms of INSTIs by examining the genetic changes in the viral genome during in vitro passaging experiments, not from clinical samples."
38427738,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,We demonstrate that INSTIs are more readily overwhelmed by high MOI than other classes of antiretrovirals. HIV-1 more rapidly acquires resistance mutations in the drug-target gene in the presence of an RT inhibitor compared to the INSTI DTG.,The paper discusses the results of in vitro selection experiments where HIV-1 variants were propagated in the presence of increasing concentrations of the INSTI dolutegravir and the RT inhibitor EFdA. These experiments involved measuring the resistance of the virus to these drugs over time.
38427738,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,No evidence,"The paper does not mention the public availability of sequences. It focuses on in vitro studies and the genetic analysis of HIV-1 clones propagated in cell lines, not clinical sequences from patients."
38427738,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No,"The NL4-3 strain used in the experiments described above is a laboratory-adapted, subtype B, CXCR4-tropic HIV-1 isolate. To extend our investigation to CCR5-tropic and primary HIV-1 isolates, we performed multiple DTG selection experiments with the subtype C, transmitted founder, CCR5-tropic isolate CH185. We previously reported that single Env mutations confer a modest replication advantage in spreading infection (45, 46). We previously reported that mutations at Env-541 and Env-558 reduce sensitivity to DTG (45, 46).","The paper does not provide GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates. It primarily focuses on the laboratory strains NL4-3 and CH185, mentioning their genomic regions sequenced but not their accession numbers."
38427738,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,0,"To elucidate INSTI resistance mechanisms, we propagated HIV-1 in the presence of escalating concentrations of the INSTI dolutegravir. HIV-1 became resistant to dolutegravir by sequentially acquiring mutations in the envelope glycoprotein and the nucleocapsid protein.","The paper does not report on individuals from whom samples were sequenced for HIV. It focuses on in vitro studies using laboratory-adapted HIV-1 strains and cell line models, not patient-derived samples."
38427738,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,No,"The NL4-3 strain used in the experiments described above is a laboratory-adapted, subtype B, CXCR4-tropic HIV-1 isolate. To extend our investigation to CCR5-tropic and primary HIV-1 isolates, we performed multiple DTG selection experiments with the subtype C, transmitted founder, CCR5-tropic isolate CH185. We previously reported that single Env mutations confer a modest replication advantage in spreading infection (45, 46). We previously reported that mutations at Env-541 and Env-558 reduce sensitivity to DTG (45, 46).","The paper does not mention the origin of sequenced samples from specific countries. It focuses on laboratory-adapted strains and their mutations under in vitro conditions, not on clinical isolates from various countries."
38427738,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,No,"To elucidate INSTI resistance mechanisms, we propagated HIV-1 in the presence of escalating concentrations of the INSTI dolutegravir. HIV-1 became resistant to dolutegravir by sequentially acquiring mutations in the envelope glycoprotein and the nucleocapsid protein.",The paper does not provide any information about the years from which sequenced samples were obtained. It centers on the lab adaptation process and the mutations acquired over nearly a year of passaging in vitro.
38427738,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"The NL4-3 strain used in the experiments described above is a laboratory-adapted, subtype B, CXCR4-tropic HIV-1 isolate. To extend our investigation to CCR5-tropic and primary HIV-1 isolates, we performed multiple DTG selection experiments with the subtype C, transmitted founder, CCR5-tropic isolate CH185. We previously reported that single Env mutations confer a modest replication advantage in spreading infection (45, 46). We previously reported that mutations at Env-541 and Env-558 reduce sensitivity to DTG (45, 46).",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It details the use of molecular clones and the sequencing of specific genomic regions without discussing cloning of clinical samples.
38427738,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"gag, pol, env, nef, vif, vpr","At the indicated time points, genomic DNA was extracted from infected cells using the DNeasy Blood and Tissue Minikit (Qiagen), and the Gag-, Pol-, Env-, and Nef-coding regions were amplified by PrimeSTAR GXL DNA polymerase (Takara Bio) and sequenced (Psomagen or Poochon Scientific) using previously described primers. HIV-1 acquires multiple mutations in the Env- and NC-coding regions during long-term propagation in DTG To investigate how HIV-1 develops high-level resistance to INSTIs, we infected the SupT1 T cell line with the HIV-1 NL4-3 clone (47) and serially propagated the virus in the presence of increasing concentrations of DTG (Fig. 1A).","The paper reports the sequencing of multiple HIV-1 genes, including *gag*, *pol*, *env*, and *nef*, during the resistance studies. These genes were analyzed to identify mutations associated with resistance to the integrase strand transfer inhibitor dolutegravir."
38427738,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"The HIV-1 genome was sequenced using a two-primer strategy by Sanger sequencing. In vitro selection of drug-resistant variants. Long-term passaging of WT NL4-3 (culture 1), (B) WT CH185 (culture 1), and (C) CH185 Env-T541I (culture 2) in the presence of the INSTI DTG. At the indicated time points, genomic DNA was extracted from drug-treated cultures, and the Gag-, Pol-, and Env-coding regions were sequenced. The TCID50 of the virus stocks was determined using TZM-bl cells. Briefly, 1.0 × 104 TZM-bl cells were incubated with serially diluted virus stocks in the presence of diethylaminoethyl (DEAE)-dextran (30 μg/ml). At 48 hours after infection, luciferase activity was measured using the Britelite plus reporter gene assay system (PerkinElmer) and GloMax Navigator microplate luminometer (Promega).",The paper describes Sanger sequencing as the method used for sequencing the HIV-1 genome during the study. This is indicated by the mention of Sanger DNA sequencing as part of the process of verifying the constructed plasmids.
38427738,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"Evista study. The primary objective of this study was to investigate the efficacy and safety of evaporated milk vis-a-vis tinidazole in 618 HIV - infected adult patients and to perform Genotypic Resistance Testing in Nonresponders only. Inclusion criteria of the Evista study were: 3. Virological failure on protease inhibitors, nonnucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors, and/or integrase inhibitors at 48 weeks.Custom 3-primer genotyping protocol 5’ End-Seq Primer (41bp)333333-′CGAATCGGGAACACAACTGAAAG C-3′33442430-15-0401-αntigivΔptprimer41bp41bp3333344243(seq)AAAA-3′33442430-15-0401-BIG-cpm-1213ctecat-cctgcgtgctcam-specmotpr 00418070135856243450-20-061901-044962VIFWINDOWPHAST-3′65-000021015125-19-016groptpr045902002000EVVPFRN04VVPBHTVVPVOCBIC6IVcrbbf160-005-CHN-15-0401-Ministeffr154242GSKNNIH015017125mgZIKOVExVxv-3′AAATAAATAACG T35e225mg3300907980362DNATCR016059601383523P41bp41bp-A-999-3′GGTTATCTCT ATTCATTCCAAACC GTCGGTGGUCGTG4480198802975uniq41bpJPROTSDOESVOINCOR0041Energy C3P0418-7-0300DA0434FERSXFIDK α-toxin αB PrB F1′(IFLSP)=IonFunct cell templateESGHTA3-kindledonniaonginguaphage255. All infections due to obstuption507470Testing014038032150 córpt C2500045- Hom0.3VSV-G-engagedG antenaarange173.int20-techONPhase-geneshyzy, tazarotene mib4741-40030co-EY5.0SH-METAMXSPEC0.000002524_don020942soccerxl valv-o-03- encap gel=IVT하 PRACEHPheD,PC2389728042ŞDnymphs!AAATAAATAACG T30-37e2CMapulcordp constructM,Yellow cable<nelsonbioin1392dsM,Yellow MaxlineTLÆA_2-4874-0210380Reverse_nameخلص_check code-attribute-attribute-H110R-MD extragonal-0gianño148-2-0aeuniversityel_EMAIL157Spanish-hinkelhABVI-IJ-05120ESGHTA3-kindledonniaonginguap2595719-150heroinlog10carbon.com)002w3University-encoding173.007151.0uP41bp41bp-GLIDE3′G-3′-3′deGàdeusa195-3iledjeJPROTSDOESVOINCOR0041Energy C3P0041811478repare.abrepair.comenergybank.gxnFiers اللبن مصنع. Experimental observation of the integral structure=IVPIC","The paper does not mention the type of clinical specimens that were sequenced, but it does state that the laboratory-adapted strains were used."
38427738,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"To elucidate INSTI resistance mechanisms, we propagated HIV-1 in the presence of escalating concentrations of the INSTI dolutegravir. HIV-1 became resistant to dolutegravir by sequentially acquiring mutations in the envelope glycoprotein and the nucleocapsid protein. The selected Env mutations enhance the ability of the virus to spread via cell-cell transfer, thereby increasing the multiplicity of infection (MOI). Our findings advance the understanding of how HIV-1 can evolve resistance to antiretrovirals, including the potent INSTIs, in the absence of drug-target gene mutations.","The paper does not discuss sequences obtained from individuals experiencing virological failure. It focuses on laboratory studies of HIV-1 propagation in the presence of inhibitors, examining the genetic changes and resistance mechanisms without mentioning clinical cases of virological failure."
38427738,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,This study does not mention any clinical trial involving patients. The focus is on laboratory experiments with HIV-1 strains propagated in cell lines.,"The paper does not mention any clinical trials involving patients. It focuses on laboratory experiments with HIV-1 strains propagated in cell lines, examining the genetic changes and resistance mechanisms without mentioning clinical trials."
38427738,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"To elucidate INSTI resistance mechanisms, we propagated HIV-1 in the presence of escalating concentrations of the INSTI dolutegravir. HIV-1 became resistant to dolutegravir by sequentially acquiring mutations in the envelope glycoprotein and the nucleocapsid protein. Our findings advance the understanding of how HIV-1 can evolve resistance to antiretrovirals, including the potent INSTIs, in the absence of drug-target gene mutations.","The paper does not mention any sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs. It focuses on laboratory studies of HIV-1 propagation in the presence of inhibitors, examining the genetic changes and resistance mechanisms without mentioning the treatment history of individuals."
38427738,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,No,"To elucidate INSTI resistance mechanisms, we propagated HIV-1 in the presence of escalating concentrations of the INSTI dolutegravir. HIV-1 became resistant to dolutegravir by sequentially acquiring mutations in the envelope glycoprotein and the nucleocapsid protein. Our findings advance the understanding of how HIV-1 can evolve resistance to antiretrovirals, including the potent INSTIs, in the absence of drug-target gene mutations.","The paper does not mention any individuals who had previously received drugs before sample sequencing. It focuses on laboratory studies of HIV-1 propagation in the presence of inhibitors, examining the genetic changes and resistance mechanisms without mentioning the treatment history of individuals."
38427738,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,No,"To elucidate INSTI resistance mechanisms, we propagated HIV-1 in the presence of escalating concentrations of the INSTI dolutegravir. HIV-1 became resistant to dolutegravir by sequentially acquiring mutations in the envelope glycoprotein and the nucleocapsid protein. Our findings advance the understanding of how HIV-1 can evolve resistance to antiretrovirals, including the potent INSTIs, in the absence of drug-target gene mutations.","The paper does not mention any individuals who had previously received drugs before sample sequencing. It focuses on laboratory studies of HIV-1 propagation in the presence of inhibitors, examining the genetic changes and resistance mechanisms without mentioning the treatment history of individuals."
38864613,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"Here, we characterized ISL and LEN in vitro to assess combinatorial antiviral activity, cytotoxicity, and the potential for interactions between the two compounds. ISL and LEN were evaluated for their ability to prevent HIV-1 infection in MT4-GFP cells as described in Diamond et al. (6). The antiviral activities of ISL and LEN against variants containing combinations of CA mutations (M66I, Q67H, or N74D) with the RT M184V mutation, a commonly reported mutation in PLWH that is associated with resistance to ISL, also showed an absence of cross-resistance.","The paper focuses on in vitro studies of drug susceptibility and resistance mechanisms of HIV-1 variants in cell culture systems, specifically using MT4-GFP cells and transfected 293T cells, but it does not mention sequencing HIV from patient samples or obtaining clinical isolates from individuals. The absence of direct references to patient samples or clinical data strongly suggests that no patient-derived HIV sequences were reported in this study."
38864613,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"Here, we characterized ISL and LEN in vitro to assess combinatorial antiviral activity, cytotoxicity, and the potential for interactions between the two compounds. The antiviral assay described above was utilized to test the antiviral activity of the combination of ISL with LEN. A matrix of ISL and LEN concentrations was tested, with each cross-titration performed in quadruplicate.","The paper reports in vitro drug susceptibility data, specifically regarding the antiviral activity and resistance patterns of the drugs islatravir (ISL) and lenacapavir (LEN) against wild-type and mutant HIV-1 viruses. The study describes the use of multiple-cycle antiviral assays to evaluate the effectiveness of these drug combinations in inhibiting HIV-1 replication in MT4-GFP cells, and it includes details on the concentrations and effects of the drugs tested, which are indicative of in vitro drug susceptibility data."
38864613,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,Sequences from resistance selection experiments have been deposited in GenBank under accession numbers PP827803 -- PP828572.,"The paper mentions that sequences from resistance selection experiments have been deposited in GenBank under specific accession numbers, indicating that the sequences were made publicly available."
38864613,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,PP827803 - PP828572,Sequences from resistance selection experiments have been deposited in GenBank under accession numbers PP827803 -- PP828572.,"The paper provides specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, which range from PP827803 to PP828572."
